parts:
- text: "My first 1D CNN baseline achieved a score of 0.5309, which is a significant improvement over the MLP baseline (0.2401). Most individual dataset scores improved, but CRI-Off saw a slight decrease.\n\nTo further improve performance, I will refine the CNN architecture by adding a second convolutional layer. This should allow the model to capture more complex, hierarchical features from the RNA sequences. I will also increase the hidden dimension of the dense layer to provide more capacity.\n\nMy next submission will be:\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deepened 1D CNN Baseline for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling\"\ntags: \"cnn, multi-dataset, sequence, deeper, architecture\"\nabstract: \"This submission refines the 1D CNN baseline by incorporating a second convolutional layer to enable deeper feature extraction from RNA sequences. The architecture includes two Conv1D layers with ReLU activations and dropout, followed by global max pooling and a two-layer dense network with\
    \ increased capacity, aiming for further performance gains across diverse RNA prediction tasks.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the deeper CNN model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512, # Increased hidden dimension for dense layer\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'conv_features_1': 128, # Number of filters for first Conv1D layer\n          'kernel_size_1': 9, # Kernel size for first Conv1D layer\n          'conv_features_2': 64, # Number of filters for second Conv1D layer\n          'kernel_size_2': 5  # Kernel size for second Conv1D layer\n      }\n\n  class SimpleCNN_V2(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 512\n      conv_features_1: int = 128\n      kernel_size_1:\
    \ int = 9\n      conv_features_2: int = 64\n      kernel_size_2: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # First 1D Convolutional Layer\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features_1, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size_1,))(x) # (batch, new_seq_len_1, conv_features_1)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second 1D Convolutional Layer\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features_2, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size_2,))(x) # (batch, new_seq_len_2, conv_features_2)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global Max Pooling across sequence length to get fixed-size representation\n          # (batch, conv_features_2)\n          x = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n          # Dense layer\n\
    \          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Output layer\n          # Handle different output shapes based on task_type\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              # Single output regression (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL)\n              x = nn.Dense(1)(x) # (batch, 1)\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # (batch,)\n          else:\n              # Multi-label classification (Modif) or multi-label regression (PRS), multi-class classification (ncRNA)\n              x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n              return x\n\n\n  class CustomRNANetwork_V2:\n      \"\"\"Custom network wrapper that implements the required interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hidden_dim=512, \n                   conv_features_1=128, kernel_size_1=9, conv_features_2=64, kernel_size_2=5,\
    \ \n                   dropout_rate=0.2):\n          self.network = SimpleCNN_V2(\n              d_input=d_input,\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n              conv_features_1=conv_features_1,\n              kernel_size_1=kernel_size_1,\n              conv_features_2=conv_features_2,\n              kernel_size_2=kernel_size_2,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize network parameters.\"\"\"\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network forward pass.\"\"\"\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the custom RNA network.\"\"\"\n      d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n      hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512)\n      conv_features_1 = hparams.get(\"conv_features_1\", 128)\n      kernel_size_1 = hparams.get(\"kernel_size_1\", 9)\n      conv_features_2 = hparams.get(\"conv_features_2\", 64)\n      kernel_size_2 = hparams.get(\"kernel_size_2\", 5)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.2)\n\n      d_input = 4 # All datasets use 4-channel input (one-hot RNA)\n\n      return CustomRNANetwork_V2(\n          d_input=d_input,\n     \
    \     d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n          conv_features_1=conv_features_1,\n          kernel_size_1=kernel_size_1,\n          conv_features_2=conv_features_2,\n          kernel_size_2=kernel_size_2,\n          dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Initial Success & Next Steps**


  Alright, so I''ve gotten a solid baseline with that 1D CNN, hitting 0.5309 – a huge jump from the MLP''s 0.2401. This is a good start. Looking at the metrics, it''s clear the CNN is performing well across most datasets, significantly improving APA, Modif, ncRNA, PRS, and MRL. The performance on CRI-Off is a slight regression, though. Both models are performing poorly on it, so that dataset might need some special attention.


  The CNN''s current form is pretty basic (one conv layer, one dense layer), so the potential for improvement is there. I''m thinking of a few avenues: deeper CNNs with residual connections, RNNs (LSTMs or GRUs), or even transformers. Hyperparameter tuning is always a given, and attention mechanisms could be integrated.


  Given the initial CNN''s success, I''ll start by making the architecture a bit deeper to see if I can push the performance up. I''ll stick with CNNs for now, aiming to see if a slightly more complex architecture can give me an edge. I also know that kernel size is important, because of the varying sequence lengths for the datasets. I am going to increase `conv_features` for the first layer, add a second conv layer, and adjust the `kernel_size`. I am increasing the `hidden_dim` as well.


  The plan is to update the hyperparameters, adding and adjusting parameters for the second convolutional layer. I''ll also modify the `create_network` function to build a `SimpleCNN_V2` with the second convolutional layer. This second convolutional layer should have `kernel_size` reasonably large to accommodate varying sequence lengths, and I''ll keep the activation, dropout, global max pooling and output layers as they are.


  I will increase the depth of the CNN.


  **Specific Modifications for Submission 2:**


  *   **Hyperparameters**: `conv_features` will stay at 128, `kernel_size` will stay at 9. I''m introducing `conv_features_2` set to 64 and `kernel_size_2` at 5 for the second convolutional layer. I''m bumping `hidden_dim` to 512 for more capacity and keeping the `dropout_rate` at 0.2, and `learning_rate` as is.

  *   **Architecture (SimpleCNN_V2)**: The input goes through two convolutional layers with ReLU and Dropout after each, a global max pooling, a dense layer with ReLU and Dropout, and then the task-specific output. The new changes focus on the addition of a second convolutional layer with adjusted `kernel_size` and `conv_features` values.


  This structure allows the network to learn more hierarchical features.

  '
