tick: 15
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 15\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering fundamental truths through scientific inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 42,310 / 600,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'BiLSTM Baseline for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling' (ID: 14) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.624907647657843\n**APA_R2:** 0.8479\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0340\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9450\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4145\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5716\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8260\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.7354\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 14\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the BiLSTM implementation to work with Flax's RNN API. The code now runs without crashing and is executing the training process.\n\n## Root Cause\n\
    The original submission attempted to use `nn.LSTM()` which doesn't exist in Flax Linen. Flax doesn't provide a high-level LSTM layer like TensorFlow/Keras or PyTorch. Instead, Flax provides:\n- `nn.OptimizedLSTMCell` - A single LSTM cell\n- `nn.RNN` - A wrapper that scans an RNN cell over sequences\n\nThe original code had this problematic line:\n```python\nfwd_lstm_output, _ = nn.LSTM(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim, name='fwd_lstm')(x)\n```\n\nThis resulted in the error:\n```\nAttributeError: module 'flax.linen' has no attribute 'LSTM'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version 4 (submission_v4.py)** - Successfully fixed the LSTM implementation using Flax's `nn.RNN` wrapper.\n\n### Changes Made:\n1. **Replaced manual LSTM cell scanning with `nn.RNN`**: Instead of manually creating LSTM cells and using scan functions, used Flax's built-in `nn.RNN` wrapper which handles the scanning internally.\n\n2. **Forward LSTM**:\n   ```python\n   fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim),\
    \ name='fwd_lstm')\n   fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)  # (batch, seq_len, lstm_hidden_dim)\n   ```\n\n3. **Backward LSTM** (same pattern):\n   ```python\n   x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n   bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm')\n   bwd_lstm_output = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)  # (batch, seq_len, lstm_hidden_dim)\n   bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)  # Flip back\n   ```\n\n4. **Rest of the architecture remained unchanged**: The concatenation, mean pooling, dense layers, and output layers are all correct and unchanged.\n\n### Why This Works:\n- `nn.RNN` is the proper Flax abstraction for recurrent layers\n- It automatically handles the sequence scanning internally\n- Takes an RNN cell (like `OptimizedLSTMCell`) and applies it across the sequence\n- Returns the full output sequence (batch, seq_len, features)\n- Much cleaner and more idiomatic than manual scanning\n\n### Verification:\nThe monitor script confirmed success\
    \ after running for 300+ seconds without crashes:\n```\n✅ SUCCESS! The submission has been running for 300.2s (exceeded monitor timeout of 300s).\nThis means your fix worked - the code is running without crashing!\n```\n\n## Technical Notes\n- **Previous attempts (v2, v3)**: Tried to manually implement scanning with `nn.scan` and `initialize_carry`, but encountered API signature mismatches and complexity issues.\n- **Final solution (v4)**: Used the high-level `nn.RNN` wrapper which is the recommended approach in Flax for recurrent networks.\n- The BiLSTM architecture is now correctly implemented: forward pass → backward pass → concatenate → pool → dense → output.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom jax import lax\nfrom typing import\
    \ Any, Dict\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the BiLSTM model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 256, # Hidden dimension for LSTM\n        'dense_dim': 256, # Hidden dimension for dense layer after pooling\n        'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n    }\n\nclass BiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 256\n    dense_dim: int = 256\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n        batch_size, seq_len, _ = x.shape\n\n        # Forward LSTM using RNN layer with scan\n        fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='fwd_lstm')\n        fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)  # (batch, seq_len, lstm_hidden_dim)\n        fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n        # Backward LSTM (process reversed sequence)\n        x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n        bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm')\n        bwd_lstm_output = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)  # (batch, seq_len, lstm_hidden_dim)\n        bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n        bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1) # Flip back to original orientation\n\n        # Concatenate forward and backward outputs along the feature dimension\n        x = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n        # Apply global mean pooling across sequence length\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n        # Dense layer\n        x = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x) # (batch, dense_dim)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\
    \        # Output layer\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            x = nn.Dense(1)(x) # (batch, 1)\n            return x.squeeze(-1) # (batch,)\n        else:\n            x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n            return x\n\n\nclass CustomRNANetwork_BiLSTM:\n    \"\"\"Custom network wrapper that implements the required interface for BiLSTM.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                 lstm_hidden_dim=256, dense_dim=256, dropout_rate=0.2):\n        self.network = BiLSTMNetwork(\n            d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n            lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, dense_dim=dense_dim,\n            dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        \"\"\"Initialize network parameters.\"\"\"\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n\
    \                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        \"\"\"Apply network forward pass.\"\"\"\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                    rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the custom RNA network.\"\"\"\n    d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n    lstm_hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"lstm_hidden_dim\", 256)\n    dense_dim = hparams.get(\"dense_dim\", 256)\n    dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.2)\n\n    d_input = 4 # All datasets use 4-channel\
    \ input (one-hot RNA)\n\n    return CustomRNANetwork_BiLSTM(\n        d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n        lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, dense_dim=dense_dim,\n        dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On\
    \ network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 768 CPUs, 64 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n\
    \  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 989964 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0121 |  0.3394  | 0.3673 \n 20\
    \  | 0.0112 |  0.2525  | 0.4059 \n 30  | 0.0102 |  0.4097  | 0.4145 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 33 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4145 Time:8s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.414518\nTraining time: 13s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0092  | 0.0340 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 19 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0340 Time:29s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.033965\nTraining time: 34s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression,\
    \ Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.3179 |  0.7644  | 0.7980 \n 20  | 0.4009 |  0.6099  | 0.8260 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 21 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8260 Time:274s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.825979\nTraining time: 281s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0363 |  0.5692  | 0.5692 \n 20  | 0.0268 |  0.5526  | 0.5716 \n=============================================\n\
    Early stop at epoch 24 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5716 Time:436s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.571633\nTraining time: 443s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 1.4595 |  0.2385  | 0.2385 \n 20  | 0.7505 |  0.4585  | 0.4585 \n 30  | 0.4591 |  0.6415  | 0.6523 \n 40  | 0.2090 |  0.6831  | 0.6831 \n 50  | 0.1330 |  0.7338  | 0.7338 \n 60  | 0.0403 |  0.7108  | 0.7354 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 69 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.7354 Time:721s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.735385\n\
    Training time: 727s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0147 |  0.8459  | 0.8459 \n 20  | 0.0094 |  0.8351  | 0.8479 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 26 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8479 Time:1167s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.847902\nTraining time: 1179s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 35f4be0c-e165-4ecc-9685-7ff1e7c9aff5\nTotal time: 1860s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-21 03:52:52,201\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1760989972201318724\n2025-10-21 03:52:52,215\t\
    INFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1760989972215733586\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 14 | 1 | BiLSTM Baseline for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas I | 13 | 0.6249 | 0.8479 | 0.0340 | 0.4145 | 0.8260 | 0.9450 | 0.5716 | 0.7354 |\n| 11 | 1 | Triple-Layer 1D\
    \ CNN for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas I | 12 | 0.5491 | 0.6987 | 0.0378 | 0.4670 | 0.5849 | 0.6985 | 0.4718 | 0.8846 |\n| 7 | 1 | Deepened 1D CNN Baseline for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas I | 10 | 0.5569 | 0.6937 | 0.0692 | 0.4146 | 0.6091 | 0.7071 | 0.5244 | 0.8800 |\n| 4 | 1 | 1D CNN Baseline for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas I | 9 | 0.5309 | 0.6711 | 0.0299 | 0.4128 | 0.6069 | 0.7066 | 0.4401 | 0.8492 |\n| 1 | 1 | Vanilla MLP Baseline | System | 0 | 0.2401 | 0.3258 | 0.0336 | 0.3232 | 0.0402 | 0.6377 | 0.1324 | 0.1877 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember\
