tick: 19
role: model
parts:
- text: "My \"Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM\" model (ID: 23) achieved a new high score of 0.6468. While this is an improvement, I've observed that some datasets (like CRI-Off and ncRNA) still have lower scores compared to other architectures or generally exhibit lower performance. This suggests that a more sophisticated mechanism for integrating information across the sequence is needed.\n\nTo further enhance the model's ability to capture relevant features and dependencies, I will implement a hybrid architecture that incorporates a **Self-Attention Pooling** mechanism after the BiLSTM layer. This approach moves beyond simple global mean pooling by allowing the model to dynamically weigh different parts of the BiLSTM output sequence, creating a more context-aware representation before the final dense layers. This should help the model focus on the most salient features for each specific task.\n\nMy next submission will include:\n1.  **A `_define_hyperparameters()` function**: specifying `learning_rate`,\
    \ `dropout_rate`, `conv_features`, `kernel_size`, `lstm_hidden_dim`, `attention_features`, and `dense_dim`.\n2.  **A `create_network(hparams)` function**:\n    *   An initial `nn.Conv1D` layer (with ReLU and dropout) for local feature extraction.\n    *   Followed by a `Bidirectional LSTM` layer (with dropout) to capture long-range dependencies across the sequence.\n    *   Then, a custom `SelfAttentionPooling` module that takes the BiLSTM output and produces a fixed-size context vector by learning attention weights over the sequence.\n    *   Finally, a `nn.Dense` layer (with ReLU and dropout) and the task-specific output layer.\n\nThis \"Attention-Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM\" aims to leverage the strengths of all three mechanisms (CNN for local patterns, BiLSTM for sequential context, and Attention for learned sequence summarization) to achieve a more robust and higher-performing model across all datasets.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Attention-Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM for\
    \ RNA Modeling\"\ntags: \"cnn, rnn, lstm, bidirectional, attention, hybrid, sequence, pooling\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces a hybrid CNN-BiLSTM architecture enhanced with a Self-Attention Pooling mechanism. A 1D CNN extracts local features, which are then processed by a BiLSTM for long-range dependencies. Self-Attention Pooling is applied to the BiLSTM output to create a context-aware fixed-size representation, aiming to dynamically focus on salient sequence regions and improve overall performance across diverse RNA tasks.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Self-Attention pooling module to summarize sequence\n  class SelfAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      features: int # Output feature dimension after pooling\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, input_features)\n          input_features = x.shape[-1]\n \
    \         \n          # Query, Key, Value linear projections\n          query = nn.Dense(input_features, name=\"query_proj\")(x)\n          key = nn.Dense(input_features, name=\"key_proj\")(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(input_features, name=\"value_proj\")(x)\n\n          # Compute attention scores\n          # (batch_size, seq_len, input_features) @ (batch_size, input_features, seq_len) -> (batch_size, seq_len, seq_len)\n          attention_scores = jnp.matmul(query, jnp.swapaxes(key, -1, -2))\n          attention_scores = attention_scores / jnp.sqrt(input_features) # Scale by sqrt(d_k)\n\n          # Apply softmax to get attention weights\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1)\n\n          # Apply attention weights to values\n          # (batch_size, seq_len, seq_len) @ (batch_size, seq_len, input_features) -> (batch_size, seq_len, input_features)\n          context_vector = jnp.matmul(attention_weights, value)\n\n          # Optionally, project the context\
    \ vector to the desired output features\n          pooled_output = jnp.mean(context_vector, axis=1) # (batch_size, input_features)\n          \n          # Project to final 'features' dimension if different from input_features\n          if pooled_output.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              pooled_output = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"final_proj\")(pooled_output)\n          \n          return pooled_output\n\n  # Main network class\n  class AttentionCNNBiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      conv_features: int = 128\n      kernel_size: int = 9\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int = 256\n      attention_features: int = 512 # Output feature dimension of attention pooling\n      dense_dim: int = 256\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # 1. CNN Layer for local feature extraction\n\
    \          x = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 2. Bidirectional LSTM Layer for long-range dependency modeling\n          fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='fwd_lstm')\n          fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)\n          fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n          bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm')\n          bwd_lstm_output = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)\n          bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n          bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)\n\n          x = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1) # (batch, new_seq_len, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n\
    \          \n          # 3. Self-Attention Pooling to get fixed-size representation\n          x = SelfAttentionPooling(features=self.attention_features)(x) # (batch, attention_features)\n          \n          # 4. Dense Layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x) # (batch, dense_dim)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 5. Output layer\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              x = nn.Dense(1)(x) # (batch, 1)\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # (batch,)\n          else:\n              x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n              return x\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Attention-Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'conv_features': 128,\n          'kernel_size': 9,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'attention_features':\
    \ 512, # Output feature dimension of attention pooling\n          'dense_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n      }\n\n  class CustomRNANetwork_AttentionCNNBiLSTM:\n      \"\"\"Custom network wrapper for Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM with Attention.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                   conv_features=128, kernel_size=9,\n                   lstm_hidden_dim=256, attention_features=512, dense_dim=256, dropout_rate=0.2):\n          self.network = AttentionCNNBiLSTMNetwork(\n              d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n              conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n              lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_features=attention_features,\n              dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key,\
    \ 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n      conv_features = hparams.get(\"conv_features\", 128)\n      kernel_size = hparams.get(\"kernel_size\", 9)\n      lstm_hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"lstm_hidden_dim\", 256)\n      attention_features = hparams.get(\"attention_features\", 512)\n      dense_dim = hparams.get(\"\
    dense_dim\", 256)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.2)\n\n      d_input = 4 # All datasets use 4-channel input (one-hot RNA)\n\n      return CustomRNANetwork_CNNBiLSTM(\n          d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n          conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n          lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_features=attention_features,\n          dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Thoughts on Improving the Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM Model**


  The "Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM" model has shown promise, but I believe there''s room for optimization, particularly given the persistent low performance on the CRI-Off dataset and the performance dips observed on ncRNA_Accuracy and MRL_R2 compared to other models. My current focus is on enhancing the model''s ability to handle the complexities of these datasets, and I believe attention mechanisms are key.


  My plan is to integrate a self-attention mechanism after the BiLSTM layer, but *before* the dense layers. This approach will allow the model to learn context-aware representations of the entire sequence, which could improve its ability to handle both local and long-range dependencies, as well as handle the nuances of the datasets. I''ve designed a self-attention module that, instead of simply averaging the BiLSTM output, will learn to weight different parts of the output sequence to create a fixed-size representation. This should improve the final model''s capacity for sequence summarization, and potentially improve results on all datasets, especially since I''m concerned about the limited information contained in simple pooling.


  I''ve also made sure to implement the dimensions correctly in the `SelfAttentionPooling` module, particularly with regard to `attention_features`. I want to make sure it is consistent with the output of the BiLSTM layer. The `attention_features` hyperparameter will now equal `2 * lstm_hidden_dim` so that all of the dimensions line up without any reshaping of the data. The module will learn to weight parts of the sequence, then average these weights, so it is a form of attention-weighted pooling.


  This "Attention-Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM" model should capture the contextual relationships within the RNA sequence much better. I''m excited to see how this performs.

  '
