parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 21\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering fundamental truths through scientific inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 67,254 / 600,000 used (11%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Attention-Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM for RNA Modeling' (ID: 30) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6541797497483631\n**APA_R2:** 0.8607\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0497\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9485\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4136\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5671\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8998\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8400\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 30\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a simple naming inconsistency that prevented the code from running.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a typo in the `create_network`\
    \ function at line 81. The class was defined as `CustomRNANetwork_AttentionCNNBiLSTM` but the function tried to instantiate `CustomRNANetwork_CNNBiLSTM` (missing \"Attention\" in the name).\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nNameError: name 'CustomRNANetwork_CNNBiLSTM' is not defined. Did you mean: 'CustomRNANetwork_AttentionCNNBiLSTM'?\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 145 in `submission_v2.py` from:\n```python\nreturn CustomRNANetwork_CNNBiLSTM(\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nreturn CustomRNANetwork_AttentionCNNBiLSTM(\n```\n\nThis corrects the class name to match the actual class definition, allowing the network to be properly instantiated.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the code is now running successfully without crashing for over 300 seconds. The evaluation is proceeding normally - it's just taking time to complete the full training/validation process, which is expected behavior for this type of deep learning task.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Original submission:**\
    \ Evaluation 30\n- **Fixed version:** submission_v2.py\n- **Fix type:** Simple typo correction (class name mismatch)\n- **Network architecture:** Attention-Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM with:\n  - CNN layers for local feature extraction\n  - Bidirectional LSTM for long-range dependencies\n  - Self-attention pooling for sequence summarization\n  - Dense layers for final prediction\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Any, Dict\n\n# Self-Attention pooling module to summarize sequence\nclass SelfAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n    features: int # Output feature dimension after pooling\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, input_features)\n        input_features = x.shape[-1]\n\n\
    \        # Query, Key, Value linear projections\n        query = nn.Dense(input_features, name=\"query_proj\")(x)\n        key = nn.Dense(input_features, name=\"key_proj\")(x)\n        value = nn.Dense(input_features, name=\"value_proj\")(x)\n\n        # Compute attention scores\n        # (batch_size, seq_len, input_features) @ (batch_size, input_features, seq_len) -> (batch_size, seq_len, seq_len)\n        attention_scores = jnp.matmul(query, jnp.swapaxes(key, -1, -2))\n        attention_scores = attention_scores / jnp.sqrt(input_features) # Scale by sqrt(d_k)\n\n        # Apply softmax to get attention weights\n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1)\n\n        # Apply attention weights to values\n        # (batch_size, seq_len, seq_len) @ (batch_size, seq_len, input_features) -> (batch_size, seq_len, input_features)\n        context_vector = jnp.matmul(attention_weights, value)\n\n        # Optionally, project the context vector to the desired output features\n\
    \        pooled_output = jnp.mean(context_vector, axis=1) # (batch_size, input_features)\n\n        # Project to final 'features' dimension if different from input_features\n        if pooled_output.shape[-1] != self.features:\n            pooled_output = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"final_proj\")(pooled_output)\n\n        return pooled_output\n\n# Main network class\nclass AttentionCNNBiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    conv_features: int = 128\n    kernel_size: int = 9\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 256\n    attention_features: int = 512 # Output feature dimension of attention pooling\n    dense_dim: int = 256\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\n        # 1. CNN Layer for local feature extraction\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 2. Bidirectional LSTM Layer for long-range dependency modeling\n        fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='fwd_lstm')\n        fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)\n        fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n        bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm')\n        bwd_lstm_output = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)\n        bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n        bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)\n\n        x = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1) # (batch, new_seq_len, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n        # 3. Self-Attention Pooling to get fixed-size representation\n        x = SelfAttentionPooling(features=self.attention_features)(x)\
    \ # (batch, attention_features)\n\n        # 4. Dense Layer\n        x = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x) # (batch, dense_dim)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 5. Output layer\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            x = nn.Dense(1)(x) # (batch, 1)\n            return x.squeeze(-1) # (batch,)\n        else:\n            x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n            return x\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Attention-Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'conv_features': 128,\n        'kernel_size': 9,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 256,\n        'attention_features': 512, # Output feature dimension of attention pooling\n        'dense_dim': 256,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n    }\n\nclass CustomRNANetwork_AttentionCNNBiLSTM:\n    \"\"\"Custom network\
    \ wrapper for Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM with Attention.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                 conv_features=128, kernel_size=9,\n                 lstm_hidden_dim=256, attention_features=512, dense_dim=256, dropout_rate=0.2):\n        self.network = AttentionCNNBiLSTMNetwork(\n            d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n            conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n            lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_features=attention_features,\n            dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if\
    \ deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                    rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n    conv_features = hparams.get(\"conv_features\", 128)\n    kernel_size = hparams.get(\"kernel_size\", 9)\n    lstm_hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"lstm_hidden_dim\", 256)\n    attention_features = hparams.get(\"attention_features\", 512)\n    dense_dim = hparams.get(\"dense_dim\", 256)\n    dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.2)\n\n    d_input = 4 # All datasets use 4-channel input (one-hot RNA)\n\n    return CustomRNANetwork_AttentionCNNBiLSTM(\n        d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n\
    \        conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n        lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_features=attention_features,\n        dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n\
