role: model
parts:
- text: "My \"Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling\" achieved a new high score of 0.6618, indicating that this hybrid architecture with attention is a strong direction. To push performance further, I will now focus on tuning the hyperparameters of this successful model.\n\nI will systematically increase the capacity of the model by adjusting key hyperparameters: `conv_features`, `lstm_hidden_dim`, `attention_dense_units`, and `dense_dim`. Specifically, I will increase `conv_features` to 192 (from 128), `lstm_hidden_dim` to 384 (from 256), `attention_dense_units` to 192 (from 128), and `dense_dim` to 384 (from 256). This aims to give the model more learning capacity while retaining the effective architectural components.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tuned Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, rnn, lstm, bidirectional, attention, hybrid, tuning\"\nabstract: \"This submission applies hyperparameter tuning to the previously successful\
    \ CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling architecture. I have increased the feature dimensions for the convolutional, LSTM, attention, and dense layers to enhance model capacity. This aims to further improve the model's ability to learn complex patterns and dependencies within RNA sequences, leading to higher performance across all diverse RNA prediction tasks.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Additive Self-Attention pooling module to summarize sequence\n  class AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      dense_attn_units: int # Hidden units for the attention scoring mechanism\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, input_features)\n          \n          # Compute attention scores\n          # First dense layer\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.dense_attn_units, name=\"attention_dense_1\")(x)\n\
    \          attention_logits = nn.tanh(attention_logits)\n          \n          # Second dense layer to get unnormalized attention weights (single scalar per time step)\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_dense_2\")(attention_logits) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n          # Apply softmax to get attention weights\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n          # Apply attention weights to original sequence and sum\n          pooled_output = jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1) # (batch, input_features)\n          \n          return pooled_output\n\n  # Main network class\n  class AttentionCNNBiLSTMNetwork_V2(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      conv_features: int = 192 # Tuned\n      kernel_size: int = 9\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int = 384 # Tuned\n      attention_dense_units: int = 192 # Tuned\n      dense_dim: int = 384 # Tuned\n   \
    \   dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # 1. CNN Layer for local feature extraction\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 2. Bidirectional LSTM Layer for long-range dependency modeling\n          fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='fwd_lstm')\n          fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)\n          fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n          bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm')\n          bwd_lstm_output = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)\n          bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)\n\n          x = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1) # (batch, new_seq_len, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n          \n          # 3. Additive Self-Attention Pooling to get fixed-size representation\n          x = AdditiveAttentionPooling(dense_attn_units=self.attention_dense_units)(x) # (batch, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n          \n          # 4. Dense Layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x) # (batch, dense_dim)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 5. Output layer\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              x = nn.Dense(1)(x) # (batch, 1)\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # (batch,)\n          else:\n              x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n              return x\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\
    \"Define hyperparameters for the Attention-Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM model (Tuned).\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'conv_features': 192, # Tuned\n          'kernel_size': 9,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 384, # Tuned\n          'attention_dense_units': 192, # Tuned\n          'dense_dim': 384, # Tuned\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n      }\n\n  class CustomRNANetwork_AttentionCNNBiLSTM_V2:\n      \"\"\"Custom network wrapper for Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Tuned).\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                   conv_features=192, kernel_size=9,\n                   lstm_hidden_dim=384, attention_dense_units=192, dense_dim=384, dropout_rate=0.2):\n          self.network = AttentionCNNBiLSTMNetwork_V2(\n              d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n              conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n              lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim,\
    \ attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units,\n              dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\"\
    , \"regression\")\n      conv_features = hparams.get(\"conv_features\", 192)\n      kernel_size = hparams.get(\"kernel_size\", 9)\n      lstm_hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"lstm_hidden_dim\", 384)\n      attention_dense_units = hparams.get(\"attention_dense_units\", 192)\n      dense_dim = hparams.get(\"dense_dim\", 384)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.2)\n\n      d_input = 4 # All datasets use 4-channel input (one-hot RNA)\n\n      return CustomRNANetwork_AttentionCNNBiLSTM_V2(\n          d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n          conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n          lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units,\n          dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Optimizing the Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM with Attention**


  I''m incredibly pleased with the 0.6618 score achieved by the "Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling." This architecture is clearly showing promise, consistently outperforming on Modif, MRL, and ncRNA, while maintaining good results on APA and PRS. CRI-Off and CRI-On remain tough nuts to crack, but the overall trend is very encouraging.


  My immediate next step is to methodically tune the hyperparameters. While I''ve been experimenting with architectural tweaks, it''s time to refine the core parameters.  The learning rate, dropout rate, convolutional features, kernel size, LSTM hidden dimension, attention dense units, and dense dimension - these all need a closer look.


  The ideal approach would be to leverage the Ray Tune integration for an automated search across a defined parameter space. However, the current submission format restricts me to fixed hyperparameter values within the `_define_hyperparameters` function.


  Therefore, I''ll have to take a more hands-on approach. I''ll manually run a small "grid search" or "random search" by modifying one or two key parameters in each submission.  My intuition tells me that the model''s capacity, dictated by the `conv_features` and `lstm_hidden_dim`, is a good place to start.  I''ll also bump up the `dense_dim` and `attention_dense_units` to allow for more complex feature transformations after the sequence processing stage.


  Specifically, I''ll try increasing `conv_features` from 128 to 192, `lstm_hidden_dim` from 256 to 384, `attention_dense_units` from 128 to 192, and `dense_dim` from 256 to 384.  This should give me a good sense of whether simply increasing the model''s complexity within this promising framework will yield further gains. This will be my next submission''s focus.

  '
