parts:
- text: "My last submission (ID: 85) failed due to a `ValueError: Incompatible shapes for broadcasting` within the `SinusoidalPositionalEncoding` module. This occurred because the positional encoding matrix (`pe`) was initialized with a fixed `max_len` but then attempted to be filled using `position` values derived from the *current* batch's `seq_len`, leading to a shape mismatch when `seq_len` was less than `max_len`.\n\nI need to correct the `SinusoidalPositionalEncoding` to generate the positional embedding matrix dynamically based on the current sequence length of the input `x`, rather than a fixed `max_len`. The `max_len` parameter itself can be removed from `SinusoidalPositionalEncoding` as it's not used to build the `pe` matrix directly, it was a constraint for the global PE table that isn't needed with dynamic generation.\n\nI will update the `SinusoidalPositionalEncoding` module and remove `max_seq_len` from the hyperparameters and network wrapper, then resubmit the corrected model.\
    \ The goal is to successfully integrate positional encoding into the best-performing Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling architecture.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Positional Encoded Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Fixed)\"\ntags: \"cnn, rnn, lstm, bidirectional, attention, residual, positional_encoding, fix\"\nabstract: \"This submission fixes a shape incompatibility error in the Sinusoidal Positional Encoding layer, which caused the previous evaluation (ID: 85) to fail. The positional encoding matrix is now dynamically generated based on the current sequence length of the input, ensuring correct shape matching. This re-attempts to integrate explicit positional information into the best-performing Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention architecture to improve learning of sequence-sensitive patterns and achieve robust performance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import\
    \ random\n  import math\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Sinusoidal Positional Encoding Module (FIXED)\n  class SinusoidalPositionalEncoding(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int # Dimension of the input features (e.g., 4 for one-hot RNA)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, d_model)\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          \n          # Create positional encoding matrix for the current sequence length\n          position = jnp.arange(seq_len, dtype=jnp.float32)[:, jnp.newaxis] # (seq_len, 1)\n          div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.d_model, 2, dtype=jnp.float32) * -(math.log(10000.0) / self.d_model)) # (d_model/2)\n          \n          # pe will have shape (seq_len, d_model)\n          pe_sin = jnp.sin(position * div_term) # (seq_len, d_model/2)\n          pe_cos = jnp.cos(position * div_term) # (seq_len, d_model/2)\n          \n          pe = jnp.zeros((seq_len, self.d_model), dtype=jnp.float32)\n          pe = pe.at[:,\
    \ 0::2].set(pe_sin)\n          pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(pe_cos)\n          \n          # Add positional encoding to the input\n          return x + pe[jnp.newaxis, :, :] # (batch_size, seq_len, d_model)\n\n  # Additive Self-Attention pooling module to summarize sequence\n  class AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      dense_attn_units: int # Hidden units for the attention scoring mechanism\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, input_features)\n          \n          # Compute attention scores\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.dense_attn_units, name=\"attention_dense_1\")(x)\n          attention_logits = nn.tanh(attention_logits)\n          \n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_dense_2\")(attention_logits) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n          # Apply softmax to get attention weights\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n    \
    \      # Apply attention weights to original sequence and sum\n          pooled_output = jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1) # (batch, input_features)\n          \n          return pooled_output\n\n  # Residual Convolutional Block\n  class ResidualConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      conv_features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic):\n          # x_input shape: (batch, seq_len, input_features)\n          input_features = x.shape[-1]\n          residual = x\n          \n          # 1st Conv layer\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name=\"conv_res_1\")(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 2nd Conv layer\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name=\"conv_res_2\")(y)\n          \n          # Project\
    \ input features to match conv_features if necessary for residual connection\n          if input_features != self.conv_features:\n              residual = nn.Dense(features=self.conv_features, name=\"residual_projection\")(residual)\n          \n          # Add residual connection and apply final activation/dropout\n          x = nn.relu(residual + y)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n          return x\n\n  # Main network class\n  class PositionalEncodedResidualCNNBiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      conv_features: int = 192\n      kernel_size: int = 9\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int = 384\n      attention_dense_units: int = 192\n      dense_dim: int = 512\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # 0. Add Positional Encoding\n\
    \          x = SinusoidalPositionalEncoding(d_model=self.d_input)(x) # Removed max_len from here\n\n          # 1. Residual CNN Block for local feature extraction\n          x = ResidualConvBlock(\n              conv_features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Output shape: (batch, seq_len, conv_features)\n\n          # 2. Bidirectional LSTM Layer for long-range dependency modeling\n          fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='fwd_lstm')\n          fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)\n          fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n          bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm')\n          bwd_lstm_output = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)\n          bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)\n\n          x = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n          \n          # 3. Additive Self-Attention Pooling to get fixed-size representation\n          x = AdditiveAttentionPooling(dense_attn_units=self.attention_dense_units)(x) # (batch, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n          \n          # 4. Dense Layer\n          x = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x) # (batch, dense_dim)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 5. Output layer\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              x = nn.Dense(1)(x) # (batch, 1)\n              return x.squeeze(-1) # (batch,)\n          else:\n              x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n              return x\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition (removed max_seq_len)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Positional Encoded Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'conv_features': 192,\n          'kernel_size': 9, \n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 384,\n          'attention_dense_units': 192,\n          'dense_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n      }\n\n  class CustomRNANetwork_PositionalEncoded:\n      \"\"\"Custom network wrapper for Positional Encoded Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                   conv_features=192, kernel_size=9,\n                   lstm_hidden_dim=384, attention_dense_units=192, dense_dim=512, dropout_rate=0.2): # Removed max_seq_len\n          self.network = PositionalEncodedResidualCNNBiLSTMNetwork(\n              d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n              conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n\
    \              lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units,\n              dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\"\
    , 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n      conv_features = hparams.get(\"conv_features\", 192)\n      kernel_size = hparams.get(\"kernel_size\", 9)\n      lstm_hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"lstm_hidden_dim\", 384)\n      attention_dense_units = hparams.get(\"attention_dense_units\", 192)\n      dense_dim = hparams.get(\"dense_dim\", 512)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.2)\n\n      d_input = 4 # All datasets use 4-channel input (one-hot RNA)\n\n      return CustomRNANetwork_PositionalEncoded(\n          d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n          conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n          lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units,\n          dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Troubleshooting Positional Encoding in a JAX/Flax Model**


  Alright, let''s break this down. That last submission (ID 85) failed, and the error log points directly at my `SinusoidalPositionalEncoding` module. The core of the problem is a shape mismatch, specifically with broadcasting inside JAX. It seems the way I''m trying to update the positional encoding array (`pe`) isn''t compatible with the dynamic sequence lengths I''m feeding the model.


  Essentially, I''m initializing `pe` to a fixed size based on `max_len`, but the actual values I''m trying to insert, derived from `position` and `div_term`, are dependent on the current `seq_len` of the input batch. This leads to an attempted assignment with incompatible shapes, resulting in that annoying `ValueError`.


  The fix is pretty straightforward: my `SinusoidalPositionalEncoding` module needs to generate `pe` *specifically* for the current `seq_len`, not the pre-defined `max_len`.  Looking at the original implementation, I was initializing `pe` to `(max_len, d_model)` and then trying to overwrite parts of it using calculations based on the batch''s `seq_len`.  Instead, I should directly construct `pe` to the correct shape from the beginning.


  I considered two approaches. First, I could construct `pe` with the correct `seq_len` from the get-go and add it to the input.  Alternatively, I could generate a `pe` table with `max_len`, and slice it to the correct `seq_len` before adding, but slicing is more cumbersome, and the direct `seq_len` approach avoids the shape issue altogether.


  The simpler, more direct method is the cleaner solution here. So, I''m going to revise the `SinusoidalPositionalEncoding` module to construct `pe` with the shape `(seq_len, d_model)`. This avoids the problematic `pe.at[:, 0::2].set(...)` syntax entirely, making the code more readable and reducing the chance of future errors. By removing the dependency on `max_len` within the module itself, I also clean up the interface. And, of course, the now-unused `max_seq_len` parameter needs to be removed from the calling function.


  This error underscores the importance of being meticulous with shape management in JAX/Flax. These frameworks are incredibly powerful, but require attention to detail to ensure everything broadcasts correctly.


  Let''s implement these changes and resubmit.  My Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention model (ID 77) was performing the best, so let''s get that positional encoding working properly. Hopefully, this resolves the issue and I can get back to training!

  '
