tick: 49
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 49\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering fundamental truths through scientific inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 196,319 / 600,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 49 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Dilated CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling' (ID: 94) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6701809994464086\n**APA_R2:** 0.8538\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0571\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9519\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4639\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5483\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8886\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9277\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 94\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed incorrect parameter name in Flax Conv layer. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code used an incorrect\
    \ parameter name `lax_window_dilation` when calling `nn.Conv()` in the `DilatedConvBlock` class (line 43 of original submission).\n\nFlax's `nn.Conv` layer uses the parameter name `kernel_dilation` for applying dilation to convolutional kernels, not `lax_window_dilation`. This caused a TypeError during network initialization:\n\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'lax_window_dilation'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the parameter name from `lax_window_dilation` to `kernel_dilation` in the Conv layer call within the `DilatedConvBlock.__call__` method:\n\n**Before (line 43):**\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME', strides=(1,),\n            lax_window_dilation=(dilation,),  # INCORRECT\n            name=f\"dilated_conv_{i}\")(x)\n```\n\n**After (line 48 in submission_v2.py):**\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\
    \ strides=(1,),\n            kernel_dilation=(dilation,),  # CORRECT\n            name=f\"dilated_conv_{i}\")(x)\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) was verified by the monitor script and has been running successfully for over 300 seconds without any crashes or errors. The network initialization and execution proceed correctly with the proper parameter name.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Model Architecture:** Dilated CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling\n- **Error Type:** Parameter naming error in Flax library usage\n- **Fix Location:** `DilatedConvBlock.__call__` method, line 48 in submission_v2.py\n- **Impact:** This was a critical bug preventing the network from being instantiated at all\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom\
    \ jax import random\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Tuple\n\n# Additive Self-Attention pooling module to summarize sequence\nclass AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n    dense_attn_units: int # Hidden units for the attention scoring mechanism\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, input_features)\n\n        # Compute attention scores\n        attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.dense_attn_units, name=\"attention_dense_1\")(x)\n        attention_logits = nn.tanh(attention_logits)\n\n        attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_dense_2\")(attention_logits) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n        # Apply softmax to get attention weights\n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n        # Apply attention weights to original sequence and sum\n        pooled_output = jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1) # (batch, input_features)\n\n        return pooled_output\n\n# Dilated\
    \ Convolutional Block\nclass DilatedConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    conv_features: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation_rates: Tuple[int, ...]\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic):\n        # x_input shape: (batch, seq_len, input_features)\n\n        # Apply a series of dilated convolutions\n        for i, dilation in enumerate(self.dilation_rates):\n            # Each conv has 'SAME' padding to preserve sequence length\n            x = nn.Conv(features=self.conv_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                        padding='SAME', strides=(1,), # Ensure stride is 1\n                        kernel_dilation=(dilation,), # Apply dilation - FIXED: was lax_window_dilation\n                        name=f\"dilated_conv_{i}\")(x)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n            x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x\n\n# Main network class\nclass DilatedCNNBiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input:\
    \ int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    conv_features: int = 192\n    kernel_size: int = 9\n    dilation_rates: Tuple[int, ...] = (1, 2, 4) # NEW\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 384\n    attention_dense_units: int = 192\n    dense_dim: int = 512\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\n        # 1. Dilated CNN Block for local feature extraction\n        x = DilatedConvBlock(\n            conv_features=self.conv_features,\n            kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n            dilation_rates=self.dilation_rates,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n        )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Output shape: (batch, seq_len, conv_features)\n\n        # 2. Bidirectional LSTM Layer for long-range dependency modeling\n        fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='fwd_lstm')\n        fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)\n\
    \        fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n        bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm')\n        bwd_lstm_output = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)\n        bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n        bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)\n\n        x = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n        # 3. Additive Self-Attention Pooling to get fixed-size representation\n        x = AdditiveAttentionPooling(dense_attn_units=self.attention_dense_units)(x) # (batch, 2 * lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n        # 4. Dense Layer\n        x = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x) # (batch, dense_dim)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 5. Output layer\n\
    \        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            x = nn.Dense(1)(x) # (batch, 1)\n            return x.squeeze(-1) # (batch,)\n        else:\n            x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n            return x\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Dilated CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'conv_features': 192,\n        'kernel_size': 9,\n        'dilation_rates': (1, 2, 4), # NEW\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 384,\n        'attention_dense_units': 192,\n        'dense_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n    }\n\nclass CustomRNANetwork_DilatedCNN:\n    \"\"\"Custom network wrapper for Dilated CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                 conv_features=192, kernel_size=9, dilation_rates=(1, 2, 4),\n                 lstm_hidden_dim=384,\
    \ attention_dense_units=192, dense_dim=512, dropout_rate=0.2):\n        self.network = DilatedCNNBiLSTMNetwork(\n            d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n            conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n            dilation_rates=dilation_rates,\n            lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units,\n            dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key\
    \ = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                    rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n    conv_features = hparams.get(\"conv_features\", 192)\n    kernel_size = hparams.get(\"kernel_size\", 9)\n    dilation_rates = hparams.get(\"dilation_rates\", (1, 2, 4))\n    lstm_hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"lstm_hidden_dim\", 384)\n    attention_dense_units = hparams.get(\"attention_dense_units\", 192)\n    dense_dim = hparams.get(\"dense_dim\", 512)\n    dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.2)\n\n    d_input = 4 # All datasets use 4-channel input (one-hot RNA)\n\n    return CustomRNANetwork_DilatedCNN(\n        d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n        conv_features=conv_features, kernel_size=kernel_size,\n        dilation_rates=dilation_rates,\n\
    \        lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units,\n        dense_dim=dense_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n\
    ✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED:\
