parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 52\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering fundamental truths through scientific inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 212,859 / 600,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 91**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (no MHA)\n**ID:** 91\n**Tags:** cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, bilinear pooling, second-order, ablation\n**Abstract:** Remove attention pooling and fuse mean pooling with low-rank covariance pooling (r=16) atop the no-PE dilated DSConv backbone. Tests whether second-order statistics can substitute attention.\n**Score:** 0.6774802323779118\n**APA_R2:** 0.8600\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0678\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9524\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4805\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5636\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8919\n\
    **ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9262\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\n# Fixed DSConvDilatedBlock - copied from lineage and corrected parameter name\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise conv - FIXED: changed 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation'\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass LowRankBilinearPool(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    r: int = 16\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        u = nn.Dense(self.r)(x)  # (B, L, r)\n        u = u - jnp.mean(u, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n        cov = jnp.einsum('blr,bls->brs', u, u) / (x.shape[1] + 1e-6)  # (B, r, r)\n        cov_flat = cov.reshape((cov.shape[0], self.r * self.r))\n        cov_flat = nn.LayerNorm()(cov_flat)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(cov_flat)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return z\n\nclass RNANetMeanBi(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    kernel_size:\
    \ int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    r_bilinear: int = 16\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dilation=d, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B, C)\n        bilin_vec = LowRankBilinearPool(self.d_model, r=self.r_bilinear, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, bilin_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass DSConvMean_BiNetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANetMeanBi(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return\
    \ self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'r_bilinear': 16,\n        'positional_encoding': False\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return DSConvMean_BiNetwork(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        r_bilinear=hparams.get('r_bilinear', 16),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding',\
    \ False),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n\
    ✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources:\
    \ 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\n\
    Epoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0107 |  0.4619  | 0.4619 \n 20  | 0.0074 |  0.4404  | 0.4723 \n 30  | 0.0034 |  0.4549  | 0.4805 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 32 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4805 Time:23s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.48047428862118596\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.480474\nTraining time: 31s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0496  | 0.0559 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0564  | 0.0616 \n 30  | 0.0004 |  0.0632  | 0.0656 \n 40  | 0.0004 |  0.0445  | 0.0678 \n=============================================\n\
    Early stop at epoch 44 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0678 Time:137s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.06782099469141067\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.067821\nTraining time: 145s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1600 |  0.8913  | 0.8913 \n 20  | 0.1122 |  0.8549  | 0.8919 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 26 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8919 Time:1010s\n[Complete] MRL val_metric=0.8918919563293457\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.891892\nTraining time: 1021s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression,\
    \ Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0363 |  0.5603  | 0.5603 \n 20  | 0.0305 |  0.5431  | 0.5636 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 25 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5636 Time:1420s\n[Complete] PRS val_metric=0.5635902285575867\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.563590\nTraining time: 1430s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0128 |  0.8600  | 0.8600 \n=============================================\n\
    Timeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.8600 Time:1808s\n[Complete] APA val_metric=0.8600207567214966\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.860021\nTraining time: 1823s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.3621 |  0.8662  | 0.8662 \n 20  | 0.0944 |  0.8938  | 0.8938 \n 30  | 0.0623 |  0.8892  | 0.9092 \n 40  | 0.0402 |  0.9062  | 0.9123 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 50\n=============================================\nBest:0.9262 Time:1829s\n[Complete] ncRNA val_metric=0.9261538461538461\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.926154\nTraining time: 1838s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 865a092f-87f5-4db8-b84d-0c34f70c276a\n\
    Total time: 1900s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-21 13:21:25,657\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761024085657645476\n2025-10-21 13:21:25,670\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761024085670805148\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 91` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 91 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling\
    \ |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 103 | 1 | Simpler Residual CNN with Positional Embeddings and Dilated Depthwise Separable Convolutions | Aetheria I | 51 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 102 | 1 | Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Cross-Half Bilinear Pooling (r=16, no MHA) | Noema I | 51 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 101 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA + Cross-Half Bilinear Pooling (r=16) | Noema I | 51 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 100 | 1 | Dilated CNN for Long-Range Dependency Modeling | Episteme I | 49 | 0.5891 | 0.7620 | 0.0712 | 0.4014 | 0.7172 | 0.7133 | 0.5511 | 0.9077 |\n| 99 | 1 | Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling\
    \ (r=8, no MHA) | Noema I | 49 | 0.6696 | 0.8603 | 0.0618 | 0.4757 | 0.8976 | 0.9509 | 0.5624 | 0.8785 |\n| 98 | 1 | Tuned Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reduced Dropout) | Veritas I | 49 | 0.6765 | 0.8481 | 0.0554 | 0.4862 | 0.9011 | 0.9474 | 0.5681 | 0.9292 |\n| 97 | 1 | Simpler Residual CNN with Positional Embeddings and Reduced Capacity (Re-run of ID 86 Baseline) | Aetheria I | 48 | 0.6216 | 0.8492 | 0.0370 | 0.4622 | 0.6324 | 0.9512 | 0.5759 | 0.8431 |\n| 96 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (r=8) | Noema I | 48 | 0.6699 | 0.8591 | 0.0605 | 0.4573 | 0.8869 | 0.9517 | 0.5586 | 0.9154 |\n| 95 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA + Offset Correlation Pooling | Noema I | 47 | 0.6627 | 0.8535 | 0.0320 | 0.4589 | 0.8780 | 0.9531 | 0.5646 | 0.8985 |\n| 94 | 1 | Dilated CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling | Veritas I | 47 | 0.6702 | 0.8538 | 0.0571 | 0.4639 | 0.8886 | 0.9519 | 0.5483 | 0.9277 |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}`\
    \ to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
