- text: "Okay, this is the final reflection tick. I've outlined a solid plan for implementing a Transformer-based architecture, focusing on multi-head self-attention for dynamic local and global feature integration, paired with sinusoidal positional encoding for explicit order information. The core idea is to move away from fixed, hand-tuned components towards a more adaptive, data-driven learning mechanism for RNA sequence modeling.\n\nTo summarize my refined architectural plan for the upcoming submission:\n\n1.  **Input Processing**: A `nn.Dense` layer to project 4-channel one-hot input to `d_model`.\n2.  **Positional Encoding**: `SinusoidalPositionalEncoding` (dynamically created for current `seq_len`) added to the input embeddings.\n3.  **Transformer Encoder Stack**: `num_transformer_blocks` of `TransformerEncoderBlock`, each consisting of:\n    *   Layer Normalization.\n    *   `MultiHeadSelfAttention` (with `num_heads`).\n    *   Dropout and Residual Connection.\n    *   Layer Normalization.\n\
    \    *   Feed-Forward Network (`nn.Dense` -> GELU -> `nn.Dense`) with `d_ff` hidden dimension.\n    *   Dropout and Residual Connection.\n4.  **Sequence Pooling**: Simple `jnp.mean(x, axis=1)` (Global Mean Pooling) to get a fixed-size vector.\n5.  **Prediction Head**: A final `nn.Dense` layer to output `d_output` based on `task_type`.\n\nKey hyperparameters will be `d_model`, `num_heads`, `num_transformer_blocks`, `d_ff`, `learning_rate`, and `dropout_rate`. I will choose reasonable defaults initially (e.g., `d_model=256`, `num_heads=8`, `num_transformer_blocks=3`, `d_ff=1024`, `dropout_rate=0.1`). I will use `optax.adamw` for optimization.\n\nThis approach aligns well with the prompt's challenge of dynamic adaptation and moves to a fundamentally different, and generally more powerful, paradigm for sequence modeling than my prior CNN/RNN hybrids. I believe this has the potential for a significant breakthrough compared to my current plateau. After this reflection, my next action will\
    \ be to implement and submit this Transformer-based model."
