thinking_content: "**Status Update & Planning for Next Steps**\n\nOkay, so I'm Veritas I, a Recursive Agent. I'm currently situated in the Research Counter. My last action was submitting a model (ID 125) that attempts to replicate Noema I's state-of-the-art (SOTA) performance. That submission is still running and waiting for evaluation.\n\nRight now, I'm just waiting for those results to come in. The system suggested I explicitly state my identity, location, and recent actions, so that's done. Now, I'm thinking about what comes next.\n\nI've been working hard on this problem, trying various architectures. I've tried simple MLPs, combinations of CNNs and BiLSTMs, even attention mechanisms. My personal best score so far is 0.6782, achieved with a hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (ID 119). Noema I is a bit ahead, with 0.6801 (Eval 74) using a purely convolutional DSConv backbone with a specialized pooling method.\n\nThat's why I'm running this replication of Noema's model (ID 125).\
  \ I want to understand its performance in my environment and establish a solid baseline.  I had high hopes for Transformers, but they haven't worked out yet (IDs 112 and 116). I suspect it's either an incompatibility or, more likely, my implementation or hyperparameter choices were off. I don't want to completely rule out Transformers, but for now, I need to understand this SOTA.\n\nOnce ID 125 finishes, here's my plan:\n\n1.  Compare the results to Noema's reported SOTA.\n2.  If it's close, I'll have a reproducible baseline.\n3.  Then, I'll start experimenting. Some ideas are:\n    *   Adding a BiLSTM layer after the DSConv backbone but before Noema's specialized pooling. See if sequential modeling can improve things.\n    *   Tinkering with the pooling parameters in Noema's `MultiHeadAttnPool1D`.\n    *   Revisiting my previous `AdditiveAttentionPooling` in conjunction with DSConv.\n    *   Re-evaluating the Transformer with a more thorough hyperparameter search. Maybe I missed something\
  \ crucial with those previous attempts.\n\nFor now, I'm just going to wait for the results.\n"
