tick: 73
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission (ID: 129), \"Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Noema's MHA Pooling (No-PE),\" achieved a score of 0.6673. This is lower than my personal best (ID: 119, 0.6782) and also below Noema I's SOTA (0.6801). The direct integration of Noema's pooling with my BiLSTM did not yield the expected improvements, indicating a potential mismatch between a purely convolutional pooling strategy and a hybrid CNN-RNN backbone.\n\nI've also noted a new archive capsule (Archive #3) from Noema I, detailing negative results with \"Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling.\" This is important information and I will read it in the next step.\n\nGiven the performance plateau with various architectural variations and direct replication attempts, it's clear that simple integration of components is not leading to a breakthrough. The divergence in performance metrics across tasks, even for SOTA models, points to the inherent difficulty of a single \"unified\"\
    \ solution.\n\nMy strategy will now shift. Instead of just combining elements, I will propose a multi-pathway architecture, allowing different types of feature extraction and sequence modeling to contribute, specifically designed to capture diverse information scales and types simultaneously. This is a fundamental architectural rethinking.\n\nI will introduce a **Dual-Pathway Network**. One pathway will focus on local, multi-scale features using a convolutional approach (like DSConv), while a parallel pathway will focus on capturing long-range global context using a recurrent approach (like BiLSTM). The outputs of these parallel pathways will then be fused before a shared pooling and prediction head. This directly addresses the need for dynamic integration of *both* multi-scale local features *and* global sequential context.\n\nMy next actions will be to:\n1.  **Read Noema I's Archive #3** on negative results to further refine my understanding of what *doesn't* work.\n2.  **Submit a\
    \ new model** implementing this Dual-Pathway Network.\n\n`/execute_action{read 3}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-Pathway Network (DSConv + BiLSTM) with Hybrid Pooling\"\ntags: \"multi-path, cnn, rnn, lstm, depthwise, dilated, hybrid, architecture\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces a novel Dual-Pathway Network designed for multi-dataset RNA modeling. It features parallel processing streams: one utilizes a stack of DSConv blocks for efficient, multi-scale local feature extraction, while the other employs a BiLSTM to capture global sequential dependencies. The outputs of these two pathways are fused and then processed by a hybrid pooling mechanism (mean + additive attention pooling) before feeding into a prediction head. This architecture aims for robust and balanced performance by simultaneously leveraging distinct feature learning strengths, without relying on fixed, hand-tuned architectural choices for specific datasets.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import\
    \ jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Additive Self-Attention pooling module to summarize sequence (from my successful models)\n  class AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      dense_attn_units: int # Hidden units for the attention scoring mechanism\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, input_features)\n          \n          # Compute attention scores\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.dense_attn_units, name=\"attention_dense_1\")(x)\n          attention_logits = nn.tanh(attention_logits)\n          \n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_dense_2\")(attention_logits) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n          # Apply softmax to get attention weights\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n          # Apply attention weights to original sequence\
    \ and sum\n          pooled_output = jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1) # (batch, input_features)\n          \n          return pooled_output\n\n  # Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (from Noema I's SOTA)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Pre-norm\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # Main Dual-Pathway Network\n  class DualPathwayRNANetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      \n      # Common feature dimension for pathways\n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n\n      # DSConv Pathway parameters\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      \n      # BiLSTM Pathway parameters - uses d_model_common for hidden features\n\n      # Attention pooling parameters\n      attention_dense_units: int = 128\n      \n      # Dense head parameters\n      dense_head_1_dim: int = 512\n      dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n      \n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common for both pathways\n    \
    \      initial_embedding = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_embedding\")(x)\n          initial_embedding = nn.gelu(initial_embedding)\n          initial_embedding = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(initial_embedding, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # --- Pathway 1: DSConv for local, multi-scale features ---\n          x_conv = initial_embedding\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x_conv = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x_conv, deterministic=deterministic) # Output shape: (batch, seq_len, d_model_common)\n\n          # --- Pathway 2: BiLSTM for global sequential context ---\n          x_lstm =\
    \ initial_embedding\n          fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.d_model_common), name='fwd_lstm') \n          fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x_lstm)\n          fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x_reversed = jnp.flip(x_lstm, axis=1)\n          bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.d_model_common), name='bwd_lstm') \n          bwd_lstm_output = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)\n          bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n          bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)\n\n          x_lstm = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len, 2 * d_model_common)\n\n          # --- Fusion of Pathways ---\n          # To fuse, we first need to ensure x_conv matches x_lstm's feature dimension.\n          # The DSConv output is d_model_common, BiLSTM output is 2 * d_model_common.\n        \
    \  # So, project x_conv to 2 * d_model_common before concatenation.\n          x_conv = nn.Dense(2 * self.d_model_common, name=\"conv_fusion_proj\")(x_conv)\n          x_conv = nn.gelu(x_conv)\n          x_conv = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_conv, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x_fused = jnp.concatenate([x_conv, x_lstm], axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len, 4 * d_model_common)\n          \n          # 3. Hybrid Pooling: Mean Pooling + Additive Attention Pooling\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(x_fused, axis=1) # (batch, 4 * d_model_common)\n          \n          attention_pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(dense_attn_units=self.attention_dense_units)(x_fused) # (batch, 4 * d_model_common)\n          \n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, attention_pooled], axis=-1) # (batch, 8 * d_model_common)\n          \n          # 4. Dense Layers for Prediction Head\n          x = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim, name=\"dense_head_1\")(x_pooled) \n          x = nn.gelu(x)\
    \ \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim, name=\"dense_head_2\")(x) \n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 5. Output layer\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              x = nn.Dense(1, name=\"output_layer\")(x)\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              x = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name=\"output_layer\")(x)\n              return x\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the Dual-Pathway Network.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common': 192, # Reduced to manage complexity and prevent token overflow\n          'ds_num_blocks': 3,    # Reduced\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4), # Reduced\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'attention_dense_units': 96,\
    \ # Reduced proportionally\n          'dense_head_1_dim': 512,\n          'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n      }\n\n  class CustomRNANetwork_DualPathway:\n      \"\"\"Custom network wrapper for Dual-Pathway Network.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                   d_model_common=192, ds_num_blocks=3, ds_dilations=(1, 2, 4), ds_kernel_size=7,\n                   attention_dense_units=96, dense_head_1_dim=512, dense_head_2_dim=256, dropout_rate=0.1):\n          self.network = DualPathwayRNANetwork(\n              d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n              d_model_common=d_model_common, ds_num_blocks=ds_num_blocks, ds_dilations=ds_dilations, ds_kernel_size=ds_kernel_size,\n              attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units,\n              dense_head_1_dim=dense_head_1_dim, dense_head_2_dim=dense_head_2_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key,\
    \ dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    \
    \  )\n\n  # Standard base seed and batch size\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
