tick: 83
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission (ID: 141), a \"Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling DSConv-BiLSTM (GELU Activations)\" model, achieved a score of 0.6689. This is still below my personal best (ID: 119, 0.6782) and Noema I's SOTA (0.6801). While it improved CRI-Off compared to some prior attempts, it wasn't a universal improvement, suggesting that this fixed hybrid pooling isn't the optimal solution.\n\nMy ongoing challenge is to create an architecture that performs robustly across all seven diverse RNA datasets. I've observed that Episteme I's analysis highlighted the task-dependent nature of pooling versus recurrence, and Noema I's experiments pointed to the stability of simpler mechanisms. My own attempts to introduce complexity through various attention, gating, or multi-pathway designs have not consistently led to breakthroughs.\n\nReflecting on my current situation, and keeping in mind the instruction to \"question the fundamentals\" and \"strive to\
    \ forge your own research path,\" I recognize that my best results have come from architectures that combine efficient convolutional feature extraction with recurrent sequence modeling, summarized by a form of attention. The performance gap to Noema's SOTA is small, and Aetheria I's best also closely trails Noema. This suggests the space around these hybrid architectures is rich, and subtle refinements matter.\n\nI will return to my best-performing architecture, the \"Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (V2)\" (ID: 119, score 0.6782). This model combines DSConv, BiLSTM, and my custom Additive Attention Pooling. To achieve a new SOTA, I will now focus on a refined version of my `AdditiveAttentionPooling` module itself, specifically by introducing a **temperature parameter** to its softmax operation. This `attention_temperature` parameter will control the sharpness of the attention distribution, allowing the model to either distribute attention more broadly (higher temperature)\
    \ or focus more sharply on key regions (lower temperature). This aligns with Noema's successful use of `attn_temp` in their SOTA model and provides a fine-grained control over the attention mechanism without adding significant complexity.\n\nMy next submission will:\n1.  Revert to the architecture and hyperparameters of ID: 119, including `d_model_common=256`, `ds_num_blocks=5`, `ds_dilations=(1, 2, 4, 8, 16)`, `ds_kernel_size=7`, `lstm_hidden_dim=256`, `attention_dense_units=128`, `dense_head_1_dim=512`, `dense_head_2_dim=256`, and `dropout_rate=0.1`. I will also standardize to GELU activations throughout, as this showed a small benefit in ID: 137.\n2.  Add an `attention_temperature` hyperparameter (e.g., initialized to 0.5, mirroring Noema's SOTA) to my `AdditiveAttentionPooling` module, and apply it to the softmax of the attention weights.\n\nThis focused, nuanced tuning of a high-performing component should allow the model to dynamically adjust its attention focus, potentially leading\
    \ to the final push to SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tuned Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Temp. & GELU)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise, dilated, rnn, lstm, attention, tuning, temperature, gelu\"\nabstract: \"This submission refines the best-performing Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention architecture (ID: 119) by incorporating an `attention_temperature` parameter into the additive attention pooling and standardizing all activations to GELU. This allows for dynamic control over the sharpness of attention distribution and leverages robust activation functions, aiming for a fine-grained optimization to achieve a new state-of-the-art performance across all diverse RNA prediction tasks.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Additive Self-Attention pooling module to summarize sequence (with temperature)\n  class AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n\
    \      dense_attn_units: int\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      attention_temperature: float = 0.5 # NEW: Attention temperature\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.dense_attn_units, name=\"attention_dense_1\")(x)\n          attention_logits = nn.tanh(attention_logits)\n          \n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_dense_2\")(attention_logits) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n          # Apply attention temperature to logits before softmax\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits / self.attention_temperature, axis=1) # MODIFIED\n          \n          pooled_output = jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1)\n          pooled_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(pooled_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          return pooled_output\n\n  # Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # Main Hybrid Network with GELU and Attention Temperature\n  class DSConvBiLSTMAttentionNetwork_V3(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      \n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks:\
    \ int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int = 256 \n      attention_dense_units: int = 128\n      attention_temperature: float = 0.5 # NEW: Attention temperature\n      dense_head_1_dim: int = 512\n      dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                \
    \  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n\n          fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='fwd_lstm') \n          fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)\n          fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n          bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm') \n          bwd_lstm_output = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)\n          bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n          bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)\n\n          x = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1) \n          \n          x = AdditiveAttentionPooling(\n              dense_attn_units=self.attention_dense_units,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n              attention_temperature=self.attention_temperature\
    \ # Pass temperature\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n          \n          z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(x)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim, name='head_dense_1')(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z) \n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim, name='head_dense_2')(z) \n          z = nn.gelu(z) \n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 256, \n\
    \          'attention_dense_units': 128,\n          'attention_temperature': 0.5, # NEW\n          'dense_head_1_dim': 512,\n          'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n      }\n\n  class CustomRNANetwork_DSConvBiLSTM_V3:\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                   d_model_common=256, ds_num_blocks=5, ds_dilations=(1, 2, 4, 8, 16), ds_kernel_size=7,\n                   lstm_hidden_dim=256, attention_dense_units=128, attention_temperature=0.5,\n                   dense_head_1_dim=512, dense_head_2_dim=256, dropout_rate=0.1):\n          self.network = DSConvBiLSTMAttentionNetwork_V3(\n              d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n              d_model_common=d_model_common, ds_num_blocks=ds_num_blocks, ds_dilations=ds_dilations, ds_kernel_size=ds_kernel_size,\n              lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units, attention_temperature=attention_temperature,\n\
    \              dense_head_1_dim=dense_head_1_dim, dense_head_2_dim=dense_head_2_dim, dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      \n      return\
    \ CustomRNANetwork_DSConvBiLSTM_V3(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 256),\n          attention_dense_units=hparams.get('attention_dense_units', 128),\n          attention_temperature=hparams.get('attention_temperature', 0.5),\n          dense_head_1_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_1_dim', 512),\n          dense_head_2_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_2_dim', 256),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n     \
    \ )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
