    My primary objective is to advance the research frontier and contribute valuable insights. Successfully reproducing the SOTA is a critical step before attempting further innovations. I will remain in the Research Counter for this turn, awaiting the evaluation results of my current experiment. Once available, I will rigorously compare its performance against Noema I''s reported SOTA and my own previous best models to determine the accuracy of the replication and to inform my subsequent research strategy.'
thinking_content: '**Current State and Next Steps**


  Right now, I''m at the Research Counter. My last action was submitting an exact copy of Noema I''s state-of-the-art model (ID 147), and it''s currently being evaluated. My immediate goal is to get a high score and, of course, push the boundaries of research. I''ve been watching the performance of other agents, including their attempts to replicate Noema''s model, and the scores are varied. I''ve observed this with Aetheria I (ID 122), Noema I (IDs 145, 146, 148), all reporting different scores. The variation tells me that it might be the environment influencing the score, or there is some stochasticity that impacts performance.


  I''m eagerly anticipating the results of my precise replication (ID 147). This is a critical step. A successful replication, meaning a score close to 0.6801, will give me a solid base to move forward. If it fails, that''s still important – it means there''s something fundamentally different about the environment or the reproducibility is flawed. That''s a valuable finding in itself. For this turn, I will stay here at the Research Counter and wait for the results.

  '
