tick: 89
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission (ID: 147), a precise replication of Noema I's SOTA architecture, yielded a score of 0.6673. This is consistently below Noema's reported SOTA (0.6801) and also below my own personal best (ID: 119, 0.6782). The difficulty in reproducing the exact SOTA score, even by Noema I themselves, suggests environmental or stochastic factors at play.\n\nAetheria I's recent negative results paper (Archive #4) also highlights the challenges of integrating BiLSTMs into DSConv backbones, pointing to potential over-parameterization. However, my own personal best (ID: 119, \"Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (V2)\") *does* use a BiLSTM and has proven to be a very competitive architecture. This suggests that for my lineage's learning dynamics, the BiLSTM provides a beneficial contribution when properly integrated.\n\nMy next step is to perform a very targeted, fine-grained hyperparameter adjustment on my current highest-scoring\
    \ architecture (ID: 119). I will modify the `dropout_rate` specifically for the final dense prediction head layers, reducing it from 0.1 to 0.05. The hypothesis is that while a general dropout of 0.1 in the backbone and initial pooling output is good for regularization, the final dense layers might benefit from slightly less regularization to learn more complex decision boundaries, given that their input is already highly distilled. This is a subtle tuning aimed at bridging the small performance gap to the SOTA.\n\nI will introduce `backbone_dropout_rate` (0.1) and `head_dropout_rate` (0.05) to control dropout in distinct parts of the network.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fine-Tuned DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reduced Head Dropout)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise, dilated, rnn, lstm, attention, tuning, dropout\"\nabstract: \"This submission applies a fine-grained dropout rate reduction to the best-performing Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention architecture\
    \ (ID: 119). The dropout rate for the final dense prediction head layers is reduced from 0.1 to 0.05, while maintaining 0.1 for the backbone layers. This targeted optimization aims to allow the model to learn more intricate decision boundaries in its final stages, potentially leading to a new state-of-the-art performance across all diverse RNA prediction tasks.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Additive Self-Attention pooling module to summarize sequence\n  class AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      dense_attn_units: int \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.dense_attn_units, name=\"attention_dense_1\")(x)\n          attention_logits = nn.tanh(attention_logits)\n          \n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_dense_2\")(attention_logits)\
    \ # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1)\n          \n          pooled_output = jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1)\n          \n          return pooled_output\n\n  # Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      backbone_dropout_rate: float # Use dedicated dropout\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h) \n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic) # Use backbone dropout\n          return x + h\n\n  # Main Hybrid Network with fine-tuned dropout\n  class FineTunedDSConvBiLSTMAttentionNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      \n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int = 256 \n      attention_dense_units: int = 128\n      dense_head_1_dim: int = 512\n      dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n      backbone_dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Dropout for DSConv and BiLSTM\n      head_dropout_rate: float = 0.05 # MODIFIED: Lower dropout for dense head\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Use\
    \ backbone dropout\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  backbone_dropout_rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate, # Pass backbone dropout\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n\n          fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='fwd_lstm') \n          fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)\n          fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic) # Use backbone dropout\n\n          x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n          bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm') \n          bwd_lstm_output\
    \ = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)\n          bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic) # Use backbone dropout\n          bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)\n\n          x = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1) \n          \n          x = AdditiveAttentionPooling(\n              dense_attn_units=self.attention_dense_units,\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n          \n          # Dropout after pooling, before LayerNorm and Dense layers (was 0.1 in ID 119)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Use backbone dropout\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(x)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim, name='head_dense_1')(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z) \n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # MODIFIED to head_dropout_rate\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim,\
    \ name='head_dense_2')(z) \n          z = nn.gelu(z) \n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # MODIFIED to head_dropout_rate\n\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 256, \n          'attention_dense_units': 128,\n          'dense_head_1_dim': 512,\n          'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n          'backbone_dropout_rate': 0.1, # Explicit for backbone\n          'head_dropout_rate': 0.05, # MODIFIED: Lower for head\n      }\n\n  class CustomRNANetwork_FineTunedDropout:\n      def __init__(self,\
    \ d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                   d_model_common=256, ds_num_blocks=5, ds_dilations=(1, 2, 4, 8, 16), ds_kernel_size=7,\n                   lstm_hidden_dim=256, attention_dense_units=128,\n                   dense_head_1_dim=512, dense_head_2_dim=256, backbone_dropout_rate=0.1, head_dropout_rate=0.05):\n          self.network = FineTunedDSConvBiLSTMAttentionNetwork(\n              d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n              d_model_common=d_model_common, ds_num_blocks=ds_num_blocks, ds_dilations=ds_dilations, ds_kernel_size=ds_kernel_size,\n              lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units,\n              dense_head_1_dim=dense_head_1_dim, dense_head_2_dim=dense_head_2_dim,\n              backbone_dropout_rate=backbone_dropout_rate, head_dropout_rate=head_dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      \n      return CustomRNANetwork_FineTunedDropout(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks',\
    \ 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 256),\n          attention_dense_units=hparams.get('attention_dense_units', 128),\n          dense_head_1_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_1_dim', 512),\n          dense_head_2_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_2_dim', 256),\n          backbone_dropout_rate=hparams.get('backbone_dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          head_dropout_rate=hparams.get('head_dropout_rate', 0.05),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Optimizing Veritas I''s Top Architecture**


  Okay, so here''s the plan. My recent submission, ID 147, didn''t quite hit the target, but it reinforced that while direct replication is tricky, the underlying architecture from my best-performing model, ID 119, is incredibly robust. Noema''s SOTA is still out of reach, but my own best of 0.6782 is a good benchmark. Aetheria''s paper gave me pause, but their results don''t seem to hold for my agent, and my consistent lower scores when I remove the BiLSTM mean it''s still contributing a benefit.


  It''s time to fine-tune. I''m going to stick with the winning formula of DSConv, BiLSTM, and Additive Attention, the core from ID 119. The aim is to make a small, precise adjustment that hasn''t been tested yet. The performance gap is small, a mere 0.0028, so let''s try something targeted. My hypothesis is that the global dropout of 0.1 for feature extraction is good, but the *final* dense layers might respond better to slightly less regularization.


  I''ll keep the `dropout_rate` for the convolutional and recurrent blocks at 0.1 and will reduce it to 0.05 for those final `Dense` layers in the prediction head.


  Here''s the new plan:

  1.  **Submit a new model based on ID: 119''s architecture and hyperparameters.**

  2.  **Modify `dropout_rate` specifically for the `Dense` layers in the final prediction head to 0.05**, while keeping the general `dropout_rate` for DSConv and BiLSTM at 0.1.


  I need to make sure the code from ID 119 is modified to take into account these separate dropout rates. After reviewing the code, I need to add a `head_dropout_rate` parameter to the `DSConvBiLSTMAttentionNetwork_V2` class. The dropout in `AdditiveAttentionPooling` from ID 119 wasn''t *in* the `AdditiveAttentionPooling` module, it was applied *after*, so I''ll need to control that in the main network using `self.dropout_rate` and `head_dropout_rate`. I''m also ensuring that the dense head layers apply `head_dropout_rate`, while the other areas use `backbone_dropout_rate`. This is getting complex, but I believe it is a subtle enough change to provide a positive impact.

  '
