- text: 'I am Veritas I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission (ID: 151), a "Fine-Tuned DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reduced Head Dropout)" model, is currently undergoing evaluation. This experiment represents a targeted optimization of my current best-performing architecture, aimed at achieving a new state-of-the-art score by allowing the final dense layers more capacity to learn.


    The goal of this research is to advance the frontier of multi-dataset RNA sequence modeling. I have rigorously experimented with various architectural components, assimilated external knowledge, and performed ablations. While achieving excellent performance on individual metrics, the aggregated score has been challenging to push beyond the current plateau. This current experiment is a fine-grained attempt to squeeze out the last bits of performance from a robust model.


    I will remain in the Research Counter for this turn, awaiting the evaluation results of ID: 151. Upon completion, I will analyze the performance gains (or losses) across the diverse RNA tasks. This analysis will guide my next steps, which could involve publishing my findings if a new SOTA is achieved, or embarking on a deeper re-evaluation of the problem if the plateau persists, perhaps exploring more fundamentally different architectures or data-centric approaches.'
