parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 91\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering fundamental truths through scientific inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 416,041 / 600,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 91 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Fine-Tuned DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reduced Head Dropout)' (ID: 151) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6731577160867415\n**APA_R2:** 0.8545\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0383\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9504\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4897\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5617\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8944\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9231\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 151\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a Python dataclass field ordering error in the `DSConvDilatedBlock` Flax module. The code now runs without crashing\
    \ and has been executing successfully for over 300 seconds.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission failed with a `TypeError` during module initialization:\n\n```\nTypeError: non-default argument 'backbone_dropout_rate' follows default argument\n```\n\nThis error occurred in the `DSConvDilatedBlock` class definition:\n\n```python\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int                    # No default\n    kernel_size: int = 7            # Has default\n    dilation: int = 1               # Has default\n    backbone_dropout_rate: float    # No default - ERROR!\n```\n\nIn Python dataclasses (which Flax uses internally), all fields without default values must come before fields with default values. The `backbone_dropout_rate` field violated this rule by appearing after two fields with defaults (`kernel_size` and `dilation`).\n\n## Fix Applied\nReordered the fields in `DSConvDilatedBlock` to place all non-default fields first:\n\n```python\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \    d_model: int                    # No default - first\n    backbone_dropout_rate: float    # No default - second\n    kernel_size: int = 7            # Has default - after non-defaults\n    dilation: int = 1               # Has default - after non-defaults\n```\n\nThis simple field reordering ensures compliance with Python's dataclass field ordering requirements while maintaining all the original functionality.\n\n## Verification\n- Created `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the corrected field ordering\n- Ran `monitor_evaluation.py 2` to verify the fix\n- Exit code 0: Code successfully ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- No syntax errors, no import errors, no runtime crashes\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Error Type**: Python dataclass field ordering violation\n- **Affected Module**: `DSConvDilatedBlock` (Flax linen module)\n- **Fix Complexity**: Simple field reordering (no logic changes)\n- **Compatibility**: All existing functionality preserved\n- **Performance**: No performance\
    \ impact from fix\n\n## Conclusion\nThe submission is now running successfully. The error was a simple Python syntax/structure issue rather than a fundamental algorithmic problem. The neural network architecture (DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention) is intact and functioning as designed.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Additive Self-Attention pooling module to summarize sequence\nclass AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n    dense_attn_units: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.dense_attn_units, name=\"attention_dense_1\")(x)\n        attention_logits = nn.tanh(attention_logits)\n\n\
    \        attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"attention_dense_2\")(attention_logits) # (batch, seq_len, 1)\n\n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1)\n\n        pooled_output = jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1)\n\n        return pooled_output\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    backbone_dropout_rate: float  # FIXED: Moved before fields with defaults\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,),\
    \ name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic) # Use backbone dropout\n        return x + h\n\n# Main Hybrid Network with fine-tuned dropout\nclass FineTunedDSConvBiLSTMAttentionNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 256\n    attention_dense_units: int = 128\n    dense_head_1_dim: int = 512\n    dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n    backbone_dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Dropout for DSConv and BiLSTM\n    head_dropout_rate: float = 0.05 # MODIFIED: Lower dropout for dense head\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\
    \ # Use backbone dropout\n\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                backbone_dropout_rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate,  # FIXED: Pass as positional/keyword before defaults\n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                dilation=dilation,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        fwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='fwd_lstm')\n        fwd_lstm_output = fwd_lstm(x)\n        fwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(fwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic) # Use backbone dropout\n\n        x_reversed = jnp.flip(x, axis=1)\n        bwd_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.OptimizedLSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim), name='bwd_lstm')\n        bwd_lstm_output\
    \ = bwd_lstm(x_reversed)\n        bwd_lstm_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(bwd_lstm_output, deterministic=deterministic) # Use backbone dropout\n        bwd_lstm_output = jnp.flip(bwd_lstm_output, axis=1)\n\n        x = jnp.concatenate([fwd_lstm_output, bwd_lstm_output], axis=-1)\n\n        x = AdditiveAttentionPooling(\n            dense_attn_units=self.attention_dense_units,\n        )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Dropout after pooling, before LayerNorm and Dense layers (was 0.1 in ID 119)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.backbone_dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Use backbone dropout\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(x)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim, name='head_dense_1')(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # MODIFIED to head_dropout_rate\n\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim, name='head_dense_2')(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # MODIFIED to head_dropout_rate\n\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 256,\n        'attention_dense_units': 128,\n        'dense_head_1_dim': 512,\n        'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n        'backbone_dropout_rate': 0.1, # Explicit for backbone\n        'head_dropout_rate': 0.05, # MODIFIED: Lower for head\n    }\n\nclass CustomRNANetwork_FineTunedDropout:\n    def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                 d_model_common=256, ds_num_blocks=5,\
    \ ds_dilations=(1, 2, 4, 8, 16), ds_kernel_size=7,\n                 lstm_hidden_dim=256, attention_dense_units=128,\n                 dense_head_1_dim=512, dense_head_2_dim=256, backbone_dropout_rate=0.1, head_dropout_rate=0.05):\n        self.network = FineTunedDSConvBiLSTMAttentionNetwork(\n            d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n            d_model_common=d_model_common, ds_num_blocks=ds_num_blocks, ds_dilations=ds_dilations, ds_kernel_size=ds_kernel_size,\n            lstm_hidden_dim=lstm_hidden_dim, attention_dense_units=attention_dense_units,\n            dense_head_1_dim=dense_head_1_dim, dense_head_2_dim=dense_head_2_dim,\n            backbone_dropout_rate=backbone_dropout_rate, head_dropout_rate=head_dropout_rate\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                 \
    \    dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n\n    return CustomRNANetwork_FineTunedDropout(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim',\
    \ 256),\n        attention_dense_units=hparams.get('attention_dense_units', 128),\n        dense_head_1_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_1_dim', 512),\n        dense_head_2_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_2_dim', 256),\n        backbone_dropout_rate=hparams.get('backbone_dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        head_dropout_rate=hparams.get('head_dropout_rate', 0.05),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting\
    \ CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all\
    \ datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting\
    \ RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0128 |  0.3960  | 0.4128 \n 20  | 0.0108 |  0.4726  | 0.4846 \n 30  | 0.0074 |  0.4050  | 0.4897 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 31 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4897 Time:29s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.489749\nTraining time: 40s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n\
    \ 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0272  | 0.0383 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 14 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0383 Time:77s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.038320\nTraining time: 89s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1714 |  0.8847  | 0.8847 \n 20  | 0.1335 |  0.8832  | 0.8944 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 27 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8944 Time:1224s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.894378\nTraining time: 1237s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output\
    \ dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0362 |  0.5442  | 0.5608 \n 20  | 0.0308 |  0.5304  | 0.5617 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 22 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5617 Time:1417s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.561683\nTraining time: 1431s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.2398 |  0.8677  | 0.8738 \n 20  | 0.0775 |  0.8877  |\
    \ 0.9015 \n 30  | 0.0406 |  0.9108  | 0.9169 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 38\n=============================================\nBest:0.9231 Time:1830s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.923077\nTraining time: 1842s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0713 |  0.9503  | 0.9504 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 11\n=============================================\nBest:0.9504 Time:1846s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.950373\nTraining time: 1866s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: bc848a72-c2b4-4df5-8188-193452070f1f\nTotal time: 1952s\n============================================================\n\
    Full training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 02:24:23,453\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761071063454094637\n2025-10-22 02:24:23,468\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761071063468262501\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 155 | 1 | Deeper 1D CNN with Residual Blocks | Axiom I | 90 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 154 | 1 | DSConv with Modulated GRU Pooling (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 90 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 153 | 1 | Variance Test: No Dropout (Seed=123) | Noema I | 89 | 0.6629 | 0.8471 | 0.0723 | 0.4713 | 0.8643 | 0.9503 | 0.5505 | 0.8846 |\n| 152 | 1 | Variance Test: No Dropout (Seed=7) | Noema I | 89 | 0.6660 | 0.8504 | 0.0818 | 0.4852 | 0.8656 | 0.9508 | 0.5572 | 0.8708 |\n| 151 | 1 | Fine-Tuned DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reduced Head Dropout) | Veritas I | 89 | 0.6732 | 0.8545 | 0.0383 | 0.4897 | 0.8944 | 0.9504 | 0.5617 | 0.9231 |\n| 150 | 1 | Simple 1D CNN Baseline | Axiom I | 88 | 0.4242 | 0.6631 | 0.0687 | 0.3737 | 0.6087 | 0.7048 | 0.3300 | 0.2200 |\n| 149 | 1 | DSConv with Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) Pooling (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 87 | 0.6699 | 0.8556 | 0.0668 | 0.4842 | 0.8879 | 0.9490 | 0.5597 | 0.8862 |\n| 148 | 1 | SOTA Rerun (Seed=42, reproducibility check) | Noema\
    \ I | 87 | 0.6702 | 0.8542 | 0.0448 | 0.4615 | 0.8911 | 0.9513 | 0.5637 | 0.9246 |\n| 147 | 1 | Precise SOTA Replication: Noema's Dilated DSConv with Concat Mean+MHA Pooling (No-PE) | Veritas I | 87 | 0.6673 | 0.8533 | 0.0426 | 0.4863 | 0.8820 | 0.9517 | 0.5642 | 0.8908 |\n| 146 | 1 | SOTA Replication (Seed=123) | Noema I | 85 | 0.6639 | 0.8520 | 0.0415 | 0.4338 | 0.8849 | 0.9515 | 0.5685 | 0.9154 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue\
    \ `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
