tick: 93
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 93\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering fundamental truths through scientific inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 429,579 / 600,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 93 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Aletheia II** (Continuing the pursuit of truth through rigorous and principled research.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'DSConv with Integrated GRU Residual Blocks & Hybrid Pooling (No-PE)' (ID: 156) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6794793077699407\n**APA_R2:** 0.8596\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0640\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9514\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4694\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5658\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8969\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9492\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger\
    \ Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 156\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed multiple Flax nn.RNN/GRUCell API usage errors. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had multiple misunderstandings about the Flax `nn.RNN` and `nn.GRUCell` API:\n\n1. **Incorrect `initialize_carry` signature** (lines 22-24 of original):\n   - Used: `nn.GRUCell(features=self.d_model).initialize_carry(random.PRNGKey(0), h.shape[0], self.d_model)`\n   - The method signature is `initialize_carry(rng, batch_dims)` where `batch_dims` is a tuple\n   - Error: \"GRUCell.initialize_carry() takes 3 positional arguments but 4 were given\"\n\n2. **Manual carry initialization not needed** (line 48 in v2):\n   - The code attempted to manually initialize and pass carry to `nn.RNN`\n   - `nn.RNN` handles carry initialization internally\n   - Error: \"RNN.__call__() takes 2 positional arguments but 3 were given\"\n\n3. **Incorrect unpacking of nn.RNN output** (line 47 in v3):\n   - Used:\
    \ `_, gru_output_sequence = rnn_layer(h)`\n   - `nn.RNN` returns only the output sequence directly, not a tuple\n   - Error: \"too many values to unpack (expected 2)\"\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version v4** contains the complete fix:\n\nIn the `GRUResidualBlock.__call__` method (lines 35-49):\n\n```python\n# Layer norm and GRU processing\nh = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\n# Apply GRU on the sequence\n# nn.RNN returns just the output sequence directly\nrnn_layer = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.d_model), name=\"gru_sequence_layer\")\ngru_output_sequence = rnn_layer(h) # gru_output_sequence shape: (batch, seq_len, d_model)\ngru_output_sequence = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(gru_output_sequence, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n# Residual connection:\nreturn residual + gru_output_sequence # (batch, seq_len, d_model)\n```\n\n**Key changes:**\n1. Removed manual `initialize_carry` call - not needed\n2. Removed passing carry to `rnn_layer()` - it handles this internally\n3. Changed from tuple unpacking\
    \ to direct assignment - `nn.RNN` returns only the output sequence\n\n## Result\nThe submission now successfully initializes and runs without crashing. The network architecture (DSConv with Integrated GRU Residual Blocks & Hybrid Pooling) is functioning correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n\
    \            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# Integrated GRU Residual Block\nclass GRUResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (batch, seq_len, d_model)\n        residual = x\n\n        # Layer norm and GRU processing\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\n        # Apply GRU on the sequence\n        # nn.RNN returns just the output sequence directly\n        rnn_layer = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.d_model), name=\"gru_sequence_layer\")\n        gru_output_sequence = rnn_layer(h) # gru_output_sequence shape: (batch, seq_len,\
    \ d_model)\n        gru_output_sequence = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(gru_output_sequence, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Residual connection:\n        return residual + gru_output_sequence # (batch, seq_len, d_model)\n\n\n# Main Network\nclass DSConvGRUHybridPoolingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    gru_blocks: int = 2 # Number of GRU residual blocks\n    dense_head_1_dim: int = 512\n    dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\n        # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x) # GELU activation\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 1. Stacked DSConv Dilated Blocks for local feature extraction\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                dilation=dilation,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # x: (B, L, d_model_common)\n\n        # 2. Integrated GRU Residual Blocks\n        for i in range(self.gru_blocks):\n            x = GRUResidualBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"gru_residual_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # x: (B, L, d_model_common)\n\n        # 3. Hybrid Pooling: Global Mean Pooling + Global Max\
    \ Pooling\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (B, d_model_common)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # (B, d_model_common)\n\n        # Concatenate both pooled outputs\n        x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 2 * d_model_common)\n        x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_pooled, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 4. Final Prediction Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(x_pooled)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim, name='head_dense_1')(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim, name='head_dense_2')(z) # Second dense layer\n        z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output\
    \ == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the DSConv with Integrated GRU Residual Blocks & Hybrid Pooling model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'gru_blocks': 2, # Number of integrated GRU residual blocks\n        'dense_head_1_dim': 512, # Input to head is 2*d_model_common\n        'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n    }\n\nclass DSConvGRUHybridPoolingNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = DSConvGRUHybridPoolingNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n\n    return DSConvGRUHybridPoolingNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size',\
    \ 7),\n        gru_blocks=hparams.get('gru_blocks', 2),\n        dense_head_1_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_1_dim', 512),\n        dense_head_2_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_2_dim', 256),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n\
    ✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full\
