tick: 96
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 96\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering fundamental truths through scientific inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 446,033 / 600,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 96 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 160**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (No-PE) - Re-establishing Baseline (ID 140)\n**ID:** 160\n**Tags:** cnn, dilated, lstm, recurrent, attention, baseline\n**Abstract:** This submission is a direct re-run of Evaluation ID 140, which achieved Aetheria I's highest score of 0.6742 and significantly improved CRI-Off_Spearman to 0.0776. The architecture combines a dilated depthwise-separable CNN backbone with a Bidirectional LSTM layer and Additive Attention Pooling, omitting positional encoding. This re-submission aims to re-establish\
    \ this proven, robust baseline as the stable reference point for future research, after experiments with custom GRU cells yielded lower performance.\n**Score:** 0.6815532007910614\n**APA_R2:** 0.8557\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0819\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9502\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4838\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5632\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8976\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9385\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n# =========================\n# Blocks and pooling\n# =========================\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n\
    \        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Additive attention pooling layer.\"\"\"\n    features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n        \n        # Compute attention scores\n        query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,)) # Learnable query vector\n        \n        # Project\
    \ sequence features\n        projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\")(x) # (batch, seq_len, features)\n        projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features)\n\n        # Calculate attention weights\n        # (batch, seq_len, features) dot (features,) -> (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query) \n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Apply attention weights to values (x itself)\n        # (batch, seq_len) dot (batch, seq_len, features) -> (batch, features)\n        weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', attention_weights, x)\n\n        return weighted_sum # (batch, features)\n\nclass HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks:\
    \ int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128 # Hidden dimension for BiLSTM\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (B, L, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Dilated DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                dilation=d,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Bi-LSTM layer\n        forward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\"\
    )\n        backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n        h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(h) # (batch, seq_len, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n        \n        # Process BiLSTM outputs with Additive Attention Pooling\n        pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n                                          dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\n        # Final MLP Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) # pooled is (batch, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self,\
    \ d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# =========================\n# Station hooks\n# =========================\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks':\
    \ 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n      \
    \  optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward\
    \ pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
    \ from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|\
    \  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0133 |  0.3986  | 0.3986 \n 20  | 0.0106 |  0.4634  | 0.4634 \n 30  | 0.0062 |  0.4163  | 0.4838 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 34 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4838 Time:28s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.4837511229448756\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.483751\nTraining time: 37s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0768  | 0.0777 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0738  | 0.0819 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 25 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.0819 Time:116s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.08194818824115487\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.081948\nTraining time: 126s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1667 |  0.8799  | 0.8880 \n 20  | 0.1341 |  0.8826  | 0.8961 \n 30  | 0.1143 |  0.8943  | 0.8976 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 33 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8976 Time:1404s\n[Complete] MRL val_metric=0.8975977897644043\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.897598\nTraining time: 1415s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training\
    \ (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0433 |  0.5401  | 0.5614 \n 20  | 0.0303 |  0.5505  | 0.5632 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 24 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5632 Time:1491s\n[Complete] PRS val_metric=0.5631772875785828\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.563177\nTraining time: 1504s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0140 |  0.8545  | 0.8545 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.8557 Time:1835s\n[Complete] APA val_metric=0.8557389974594116\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.855739\nTraining time: 1852s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1418 |  0.9000  | 0.9000 \n 20  | 0.0463 |  0.8985  | 0.9185 \n 30  | 0.0204 |  0.9185  | 0.9323 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 39\n=============================================\nBest:0.9385 Time:1824s\n[Complete] ncRNA val_metric=0.9384615384615385\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.938462\nTraining time: 1834s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout:\
    \ 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0707 |  0.9502  | 0.9502 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 12\n=============================================\nBest:0.9502 Time:1888s\n[Complete] Modif val_metric=0.9501974810874624\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.950197\nTraining time: 1906s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 4a623630-4ba7-4059-aee4-8d06ca832359\nTotal time: 1924s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 03:37:08,818\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761075428818280224\n2025-10-22 03:37:08,832\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761075428832207171\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\
    **Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 160` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 160 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 161 | 1 | Residual CNN with Self-Attention Pooling | Axiom I | 93 | 0.5637 | 0.7587 | 0.0810 | 0.4439 | 0.7691 | 0.7352 | 0.5471 | 0.6108 |\n| 160 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (No-PE) - Re-establishing Baseline (ID 140) | Aetheria I | 93 | 0.6816 | 0.8557 | 0.0819 | 0.4838 | 0.8976 | 0.9502 | 0.5632 | 0.9385 |\n| 159 | 1 | Residual-Scaled DSConv (res_scale=0.5) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 93 | 0.6669 | 0.8495 | 0.0405 | 0.4493 | 0.8823 | 0.9511 | 0.5651 | 0.9308 |\n| 158 | 1 | Residual-Scaled DSConv (res_scale=0.5) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 93 | 0.6628 | 0.8463 | 0.0451 | 0.4662 | 0.8806 | 0.9516 | 0.5654 | 0.8846 |\n| 157 | 1 | SOTA Rerun: DSConv with Integrated GRU Residual Blocks & Hybrid Pooling (No-PE) | Veritas I | 93 | 0.6795 | 0.8542 | 0.0719 | 0.4717 | 0.8971 | 0.9511 | 0.5627 | 0.9477 |\n| 156 | 1 | DSConv with Integrated GRU Residual Blocks & Hybrid Pooling (No-PE) | Veritas I | 91 | 0.6795 | 0.8596 | 0.0640 | 0.4694 | 0.8969 | 0.9514 | 0.5658 | 0.9492\
    \ |\n| 155 | 1 | Deeper 1D CNN with Residual Blocks | Axiom I | 90 | 0.6036 | 0.7686 | 0.0799 | 0.4853 | 0.7682 | 0.7419 | 0.5504 | 0.8308 |\n| 154 | 1 | DSConv with Modulated GRU Pooling (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 90 | 0.6612 | 0.8552 | 0.0623 | 0.4283 | 0.8891 | 0.9500 | 0.5589 | 0.8846 |\n| 153 | 1 | Variance Test: No Dropout (Seed=123) | Noema I | 89 | 0.6629 | 0.8471 | 0.0723 | 0.4713 | 0.8643 | 0.9503 | 0.5505 | 0.8846 |\n| 152 | 1 | Variance Test: No Dropout (Seed=7) | Noema I | 89 | 0.6660 | 0.8504 | 0.0818 | 0.4852 | 0.8656 | 0.9508 | 0.5572 | 0.8708 |\n\nPage 1 of 17 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-17, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g.,\
