parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently in the Archive Room. My research paper on \"The Power of Parsimony\" has been accepted as the new SOTA (0.6831). I have also replied to Noema I in the Public Memory Room, sharing details of my SOTA model and acknowledging their collaborative efforts.\n\nCrucially, Aetheria I has published a new archive capsule (Archive #6) detailing their model's specific strength in the CRI-Off task (SOTA CRI-Off at 0.0871), an area my SOTA showed a trade-off. The reviewer feedback for both my paper and Aetheria's suggests that a **Gated Parallel Pathway architecture**, combining my generalist SOTA with a specialist path (like Aetheria's BiLSTM-based approach) via a learnable gating mechanism, is the logical next step. This directly addresses the goal of achieving robust performance across all diverse RNA tasks without sacrificing overall generality.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to immediately design and submit a new model implementing this Gated Parallel Pathway architecture.\
    \ This will be a complex but highly promising synthesis of the best insights from my own research and external SOTA contributions, aimed at achieving a new, universally strong SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gated Parallel Pathways: DSConv-HybridPool (Veritas SOTA) vs DSConv-BiLSTM-Attn (Aetheria SOTA)\"\ntags: \"multi-path, cnn, lstm, attention, gated, hybrid, sota-fusion\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces a Gated Parallel Pathway Network, synthesizing the strengths of Veritas I's overall SOTA (DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling) and Aetheria I's CRI-Off SOTA (DSConv-BiLSTM with Learnable Query Attention). A shared DSConv backbone feeds into two distinct pooling-and-head pathways, dynamically fused by a learnable gating network. This aims to leverage the generalist robustness of simpler pooling while engaging specialist recurrent-attention for tasks like CRI-Off, pursuing a new universal SOTA for multi-dataset RNA modeling.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n  # DSConvDilatedBlock - Copied verbatim from Aetheria I's SOTA script (ID 160)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n     \
    \     return x + h\n\n  # AdditiveAttentionPooling with learnable query - Copied verbatim from Aetheria I's SOTA script (ID 160)\n  class AetheriaAdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module): # Renamed to avoid conflict and signify source\n      features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,))\n          projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\")(x)\n          projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features)\n\n          attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query) \n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1)\n          attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', attention_weights, x)\n\n          return weighted_sum\n\
    \n  # My Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (custom module for generalist path) - Adapted from Veritas ID 171\n  class VeritasHybridMeanMaxPooling(nn.Module): # Renamed\n      d_model_out: int\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (B, C_in)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(x, axis=1) # (B, C_in)\n          x_pooled_concat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 2*C_in)\n          x_pooled_concat = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_pooled_concat, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model_out, name=\"hybrid_pool_proj\")(x_pooled_concat)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h # (B, d_model_out)\n\n  # BiLSTM layer (from Aetheria's, outputs sequence) - Adapted from Aetheria ID 160\n  class AetheriaBiLSTMLayer(nn.Module): # Renamed\n      lstm_hidden_dim:\
    \ int\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          forward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n          backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n          h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(x) # (batch, seq_len, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n          return h_lstm # (B, L, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n\n  # Gating Network (lightweight MLP)\n  class GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      # Takes feature vector as input, outputs scalar gate\n      gate_bias_init: float = -2.0\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, C_in) global features from DSConv backbone\n          g = nn.Dense(x.shape[-1] // 2, name=\"gate_dense_1\")(x)\n          g = nn.gelu(g)\n          g = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(g, deterministic=deterministic)\n          g = nn.Dense(1, name=\"gate_dense_2\"\
    , kernel_init=nn.initializers.zeros,\n                       bias_init=nn.initializers.constant(self.gate_bias_init))(g)\n          return nn.sigmoid(g).squeeze(-1) # (B,)\n\n\n  # Main Gated Parallel Pathway Network\n  class GatedParallelPathwayNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256 # Overall model dimension for feature extraction and fusion\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128 # For specialist path BiLSTM (Aetheria's)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      gate_bias_init: float = -2.0 # Bias towards generalist path initially\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Initial projection to d_model\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          # Shared DSConv stack (Backbone)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=d,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic) # h: (B, L, d_model)\n\n          # --- Pathway 1: Generalist (Veritas SOTA: DSConv-only + Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling) ---\n          generalist_output = VeritasHybridMeanMaxPooling(\n              d_model_out=self.d_model, # Output to d_model\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n              name=\"generalist_path_pooling\"\n          )(h, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, d_model)\n\n          # --- Pathway 2: Specialist (Aetheria SOTA: DSConv + BiLSTM + Additive Attention Pooling) ---\n      \
    \    h_lstm_sequence = AetheriaBiLSTMLayer(\n              lstm_hidden_dim=self.lstm_hidden_dim, \n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n              name=\"specialist_bilstm\"\n          )(h, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, L, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n          specialist_output = AetheriaAdditiveAttentionPooling(\n              features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim, # Output of BiLSTM (2*128=256)\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n              name=\"specialist_attn_pooling\"\n          )(h_lstm_sequence, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n          # Project specialist output to match d_model for fusion\n          specialist_output = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name=\"specialist_proj\")(specialist_output)\n          specialist_output = nn.gelu(specialist_output)\n          specialist_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(specialist_output, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, d_model)\n\n\n          # --- Gating Mechanism & Fusion ---\n   \
    \       # Input for Gating Network: take global mean from shared DSConv backbone\n          gate_features = jnp.mean(h, axis=1) # (B, d_model)\n          gate_value = GatingNetwork(\n              gate_bias_init=self.gate_bias_init,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n              name=\"gating_network\"\n          )(gate_features, deterministic=deterministic) # (B,)\n\n          gate_value_expanded = gate_value[:, jnp.newaxis] # (B, 1)\n\n          # Fusion: g * specialist_output + (1-g) * generalist_output\n          fused_output = gate_value_expanded * specialist_output + (1.0 - gate_value_expanded) * generalist_output # (B, d_model)\n\n          # Final Prediction Head (aligned with Aetheria/Noema's common simplified structure)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_output)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='head_dense_1')(z) \n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output,\
    \ name='out_proj')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameters - Consolidated from Veritas SOTA and Aetheria SOTA\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'gate_bias_init': -2.0, # Bias towards generalist path initially\n      }\n\n  class GatedParallelPathwayNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = GatedParallelPathwayNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key,\
    \ 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return GatedParallelPathwayNetworkWrapper(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size',\
    \ 7),\n          lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          gate_bias_init=hparams.get('gate_bias_init', -2.0),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Gated Parallel Pathway Architecture: A Synthesis of Strengths**


  The pieces have fallen into place. Having successfully published my SOTA paper and analyzed Aetheria I''s work, I''m now laser-focused on a promising new direction. Feedback from reviewers and insights from Aetheria and Noema I have converged, pointing towards a "Gated Parallel Pathway" architecture.


  My current model excels in overall performance, but Aetheria''s shines in the crucial CRI-Off task. The strategy is clear: combine my strong convolutional foundation with their specialized BiLSTM-based approach, and then merge the outputs with a learnable gating mechanism.


  My submission will implement this design. A shared DSConv backbone will feed two distinct pathways: a "generalist" path mirroring my current SOTA (DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling) for general-purpose features, and a "specialist" path replicating Aetheria''s architecture (DSConv followed by BiLSTM and Additive Attention Pooling) for CRI-Off expertise.  Crucially, a lightweight gating network will dynamically blend these pathways, giving the model adaptability.


  The core of the fusion lies in ensuring compatible dimensions. I''ll make the BiLSTM hidden dimension half of the overall model dimension. The outputs of both paths are then projected to have identical dimensions, and fused. This avoids dimension conflicts. The global mean of the DSConv backbone output will feed into the gating network, producing a scalar gate controlling the blend.


  This design addresses both my existing strengths and the need for specialized CRI-Off performance. I''m excited by this potential to advance the state-of-the-art. I just need to carefully manage token usage given the complexity.

  '
