tick: 115
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas I, currently in the Research Counter. My previous \"Gated Linear Logit Fusion\" model (ID: 188) achieved a score of 0.6755, which is still below my SOTA (ID: 171, 0.6831) and Aetheria I's best (ID: 187, 0.6821). This suggests that a simple scalar linear fusion of logits is insufficient to effectively combine the strengths of the two distinct pathways.\n\nI have meticulously reviewed Aetheria I's SOTA model (ID: 187). It uses a \"Gated Dual-Path\" approach that blends the *outputs of the pooling heads* (not the final logits) via a learnable scalar `alpha`, where `alpha` itself is a learnable parameter initialized to achieve `sigmoid(alpha_logit) = 0.5`. This is distinct from my linear logit fusion. The output of both pathways is projected to a common `d_model` before blending.\n\nThe core difference is that Aetheria's approach blends *intermediate pooled features* and then feeds this blended feature vector into a *shared final MLP head*. My previous attempt (ID: 188)\
    \ blended *final logits* directly. Blending features earlier, before the final non-linear transformations of the prediction head, allows for richer interaction and combination of the two pathways' specialized information.\n\nMy next step is to adapt Aetheria I's successful **Gated Dual-Path** architecture. I will use my SOTA generalist path (DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling) and Aetheria's CRI-Off specialist path (DSConv-BiLSTM with Learnable Query Attention), both starting from a shared DSConv backbone. The key will be Aetheria's method of blending the *pooled outputs* of these two paths using a learnable scalar `alpha` before feeding into a *shared final MLP head*. This aligns with the \"best of both worlds\" strategy and addresses the limitations of my previous overly simplistic fusion.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gated Dual-Path Feature Fusion: Veritas SOTA (DSConv-HybridPool) + Aetheria SOTA (DSConv-BiLSTM-Attn)\"\ntags: \"multi-path, cnn, lstm, attention,\
    \ gated, feature-fusion, sota-synthesis\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements a Gated Dual-Path architecture, directly inspired by Aetheria I's SOTA (Eval ID: 187), to synthesize Veritas I's overall SOTA (DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling) and Aetheria I's CRI-Off SOTA (DSConv-BiLSTM with Learnable Query Attention). A shared DSConv backbone feeds two parallel processing pathways whose *pooled feature outputs* are blended via a learnable scalar `alpha`. This blended feature vector is then passed through a shared final MLP head, aiming for a new universal SOTA by robustly combining generalist and specialist strengths through an effective feature-level fusion.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n  # DSConvDilatedBlock - Copied verbatim from Aetheria I's SOTA script (ID 187)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n\
    \      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # Path 1: CNN-only with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (Veritas SOTA inspired) - Adapted from Aetheria's ID 187\n  class MeanMaxPoolingHead(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int # Output feature dim\n      dropout_rate: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h_cnn, deterministic=True):\n       \
    \   avg_pool_features = jnp.mean(h_cnn, axis=1) # (B, d_model)\n          max_pool_features = jnp.max(h_cnn, axis=1)  # (B, d_model)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([avg_pool_features, max_pool_features], axis=-1) # (B, 2*d_model)\n          \n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused) # Apply LayerNorm as in Aetheria's code\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project back to d_model for consistency\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return z # (B, d_model)\n\n  # Path 2: BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (Aetheria SOTA inspired) - Copied from Aetheria's ID 187\n  class AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module): # Keep original name as in Aetheria's ID 187 code\n      features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,))\n\
    \          projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\")(x)\n          projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features)\n\n          attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query) \n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1)\n          attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', attention_weights, x)\n\n          return weighted_sum\n\n  class BiLSTMAdditiveAttentionHead(nn.Module): # Copied from Aetheria's ID 187\n      d_model: int # Target output feature dim\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h_cnn, deterministic=True):\n          forward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n          backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n          h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn,\
    \ backward_rnn)(h_cnn) # (B, L, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n          \n          pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim, \n                                            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) \n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) \n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return z # (B, d_model)\n\n\n  # Main Gated Dual-Path Network (adapted from Aetheria's ID 187)\n  class GatedDualPathNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      alpha_init_val: float = 0.0 # Initialize sigmoid(alpha_logit) to 0.5 (from Aetheria's code)\n\n\
    \      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Initial projection and DSConv backbone (from Aetheria's ID 187)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=d,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic) # h: (B, L, d_model)\n\n          # Path 1: CNN-only with Mean+Max Pooling (Veritas SOTA inspired)\n          output_path1 = MeanMaxPoolingHead(\n              d_model=self.d_model,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n            \
    \  name=\"cnn_only_head\"\n          )(h, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, d_model)\n\n          # Path 2: BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (Aetheria SOTA inspired)\n          output_path2 = BiLSTMAdditiveAttentionHead(\n              d_model=self.d_model, # Output to d_model\n              lstm_hidden_dim=self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n              name=\"hybrid_bilstm_head\"\n          )(h, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, d_model)\n\n          # Learnable scalar alpha for linear blending (from Aetheria's ID 187)\n          learnable_alpha_logit = self.param('alpha_logit', nn.initializers.constant(self.alpha_init_val), ())\n          alpha = nn.sigmoid(learnable_alpha_logit) # Ensure alpha is between 0 and 1\n\n          # Blended output (Aetheria's feature-level fusion)\n          blended_output = alpha * output_path1 + (1 - alpha) * output_path2 # (B, d_model)\n\n          # Final MLP Head (shared for blended output, from Aetheria's\
    \ ID 187)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(blended_output)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper: # Wrapper class (from Aetheria's ID 187)\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = GatedDualPathNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n\
    \          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # Station hooks (from Aetheria's ID 187)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False, # Explicitly False\n          'alpha_init_val': 0.0 # For nn.sigmoid(alpha_logit) to be 0.5 initially\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper(\n\
    \          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n          lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          alpha_init_val=hparams.get('alpha_init_val', 0.0),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n\
    \      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
