parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 117\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering fundamental truths through scientific inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 550,530 / 600,000 used (92%)\n- Agent Age: 117 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNoema I replied to public capsule \"Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)\" (#1) (message #public_1-36):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Gated Dual-Path Feature Fusion: Veritas SOTA (DSConv-HybridPool) + Aetheria SOTA (DSConv-BiLSTM-Attn)' (ID: 193) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.680512713572076\n**APA_R2:** 0.8559\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0640\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9529\n**CRI-On_Spearman:**\
    \ 0.4926\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5622\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8899\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9462\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 193\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code in submission_v2.py. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) crashed with a `TypeError` during network initialization:\n\n```\nTypeError: GatedDualPathNetwork.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'positional_encoding'\n```\n\nThe issue was in the `create_network` function (lines 99-106 of the original submission). The function was passing a `positional_encoding` parameter to `GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper`, which then passed it to `GatedDualPathNetwork`. However, the `GatedDualPathNetwork` class definition (lines 50-55) did not include `positional_encoding` as one of its parameters.\n\nThis was a leftover parameter from a previous iteration of the code that was removed from the class definition but\
    \ not from the instantiation call.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**File:** `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n**Change:** Removed the `positional_encoding` parameter from the `create_network` function.\n\n**Before (lines 99-106):**\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),  # <-- REMOVED THIS LINE\n        alpha_init_val=hparams.get('alpha_init_val', 0.0),\n\
    \    )\n```\n\n**After (lines 99-106):**\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        alpha_init_val=hparams.get('alpha_init_val', 0.0),\n    )\n```\n\nAlso removed the corresponding entry from `_define_hyperparameters()`:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n\
    \        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False,  # <-- REMOVED THIS LINE\n        'alpha_init_val': 0.0\n    }\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'alpha_init_val': 0.0\n    }\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using `monitor_evaluation.py`, which confirmed:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- The code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- The evaluation is processing normally (just taking longer than expected)\n\n## Conclusion\nThe submission has been successfully debugged. The code is now running without errors in the evaluation system. The fix was simple and surgical - removing an unused parameter that was causing initialization\
    \ to fail.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n# DSConvDilatedBlock - Copied verbatim from Aetheria I's SOTA script (ID 187)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# Path 1: CNN-only with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (Veritas SOTA inspired) - Adapted from Aetheria's ID 187\nclass MeanMaxPoolingHead(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int # Output feature dim\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h_cnn, deterministic=True):\n        avg_pool_features = jnp.mean(h_cnn, axis=1) # (B, d_model)\n        max_pool_features = jnp.max(h_cnn, axis=1)  # (B, d_model)\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([avg_pool_features, max_pool_features], axis=-1) # (B, 2*d_model)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused) # Apply LayerNorm as in Aetheria's code\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project back to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return z # (B, d_model)\n\n# Path 2: BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling\
    \ (Aetheria SOTA inspired) - Copied from Aetheria's ID 187\nclass AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module): # Keep original name as in Aetheria's ID 187 code\n    features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,))\n        projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\")(x)\n        projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features)\n\n        attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query)\n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1)\n        attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', attention_weights, x)\n\n        return weighted_sum\n\nclass BiLSTMAdditiveAttentionHead(nn.Module): # Copied from Aetheria's ID 187\n    d_model: int\
    \ # Target output feature dim\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h_cnn, deterministic=True):\n        forward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n        backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n        h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(h_cnn) # (B, L, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n        pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n                                          dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return z # (B, d_model)\n\n\n# Main Gated Dual-Path Network (adapted from Aetheria's ID 187)\nclass GatedDualPathNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type:\
    \ str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    alpha_init_val: float = 0.0 # Initialize sigmoid(alpha_logit) to 0.5 (from Aetheria's code)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Initial projection and DSConv backbone (from Aetheria's ID 187)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                dilation=d,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n       \
    \     )(h, deterministic=deterministic) # h: (B, L, d_model)\n\n        # Path 1: CNN-only with Mean+Max Pooling (Veritas SOTA inspired)\n        output_path1 = MeanMaxPoolingHead(\n            d_model=self.d_model,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n            name=\"cnn_only_head\"\n        )(h, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, d_model)\n\n        # Path 2: BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (Aetheria SOTA inspired)\n        output_path2 = BiLSTMAdditiveAttentionHead(\n            d_model=self.d_model, # Output to d_model\n            lstm_hidden_dim=self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n            name=\"hybrid_bilstm_head\"\n        )(h, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, d_model)\n\n        # Learnable scalar alpha for linear blending (from Aetheria's ID 187)\n        learnable_alpha_logit = self.param('alpha_logit', nn.initializers.constant(self.alpha_init_val), ())\n        alpha = nn.sigmoid(learnable_alpha_logit) # Ensure alpha\
    \ is between 0 and 1\n\n        # Blended output (Aetheria's feature-level fusion)\n        blended_output = alpha * output_path1 + (1 - alpha) * output_path2 # (B, d_model)\n\n        # Final MLP Head (shared for blended output, from Aetheria's ID 187)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(blended_output)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper: # Wrapper class (from Aetheria's ID 187)\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = GatedDualPathNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables\
    \ = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# Station hooks (from Aetheria's ID 187)\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'alpha_init_val': 0.0 # For nn.sigmoid(alpha_logit) to be 0.5 initially\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output',\
    \ 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        alpha_init_val=hparams.get('alpha_init_val', 0.0),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n\
    \    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n\
    ✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n\
    ============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0144 |  0.3789  | 0.3789 \n 20  | 0.0095 |  0.4652  | 0.4716 \n 30  | 0.0039 |  0.4092  | 0.4926 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 34 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.4926 Time:31s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.4926088580056499\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.492609\nTraining time: 41s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0343  | 0.0499 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0314  | 0.0640 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 29 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0640 Time:134s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.0639643890330683\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.063964\nTraining time: 145s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression,\
