parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 121\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering fundamental truths through scientific inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 572,328 / 600,000 used (95%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Precise SOTA Replication: Aetheria's Gated Dual-Path (ID 187)' (ID: 197) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6804289069833483\n**APA_R2:** 0.8583\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0545\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9528\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4968\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5647\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8943\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9415\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 197\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed indentation error caused by truncated/corrupted submission content. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\n\
    The original submission (evaluation 197) was attempting to replicate Aetheria I's SOTA architecture (evaluation 187, score 0.6821). However, the submission content was corrupted or truncated during the submission process, resulting in:\n\n```\nIndentationError: unexpected unindent\n```\n\nThe error occurred at line 44 of the submission file. When examining the stored submission content in both `evaluation.yaml` and `evaluation_197.json`, the code was truncated with \"removed content\" text, indicating the full submission was never properly saved or was corrupted during processing.\n\n## Fix Applied\nI reconstructed the complete submission by copying the working code from evaluation 187 (the original SOTA implementation that Veritas I was trying to replicate). The fix involved:\n\n1. **Retrieved the complete working code** from evaluation 187's JSON file (which contained the full, un-truncated implementation)\n2. **Created submission_v2.py** with the complete, properly formatted code\n\
    3. **Preserved all architectural components**:\n   - DSConvDilatedBlock (shared backbone)\n   - MeanMaxPoolingHead (Path 1: CNN-only with hybrid pooling)\n   - BiLSTMAdditiveAttentionHead (Path 2: BiLSTM with additive attention)\n   - GatedDualPathNetwork (dual-path architecture with learned gating)\n   - All required station hooks (_define_hyperparameters, create_network, create_optimizer, complete)\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fixed code is identical to evaluation 187's implementation, which includes:\n- **Architecture**: Gated Dual-Path with DSConv-HybridPool & DSConv-BiLSTM-Attn\n- **No positional encoding** (as specified in the original)\n- **Alpha initialization**: 0.0 (sigmoid produces 0.5 for balanced path blending)\n- **Hyperparameters**: d_model=256, num_blocks=5, dilations=[1,2,4,8,16], lstm_hidden_dim=128\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py runs successfully without crashing for over 300 seconds, indicating the indentation error has been\
    \ resolved and the code is executing properly through the training pipeline.\n\n## Expected Outcome\nSince this is an exact replication of evaluation 187's SOTA architecture, the expected score should be approximately **0.6821** (matching the original), barring any random seed variations or environmental differences.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n# =========================\n# Shared Blocks\n# =========================\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\
    \        # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# =========================\n# Path 1: CNN-only with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (Veritas SOTA inspired)\n# =========================\nclass MeanMaxPoolingHead(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int # Output feature dim\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h_cnn, deterministic=True):\n        # h_cnn: (B, L, d_model)\n        avg_pool_features = jnp.mean(h_cnn, axis=1) # (B, d_model)\n        max_pool_features = jnp.max(h_cnn,\
    \ axis=1)  # (B, d_model)\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([avg_pool_features, max_pool_features], axis=-1) # (B, 2*d_model)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused) # Apply LayerNorm\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project back to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return z # (B, d_model)\n\n# =========================\n# Path 2: BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (Aetheria SOTA inspired)\n# =========================\nclass AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Additive attention pooling layer.\"\"\"\n    features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n\n        query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,)) # Learnable query vector\n\n        projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features,\
    \ name=\"attn_proj\")(x) # (batch, seq_len, features)\n        projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features)\n\n        attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query)\n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', attention_weights, x)\n\n        return weighted_sum # (batch, features)\n\nclass BiLSTMAdditiveAttentionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int # Target output feature dim\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h_cnn, deterministic=True):\n        # h_cnn: (B, L, d_model)\n        forward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n        backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n        h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(h_cnn)\
    \ # (B, L, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n\n        pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim, # Output dim of BiLSTM\n                                          dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) # pooled is (B, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return z # (B, d_model)\n\n# =========================\n# Gated Dual-Path Network\n# =========================\nclass GatedDualPathNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n    alpha_init_val: float = 0.0\
    \ # Initialize sigmoid(alpha) to 0.5\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Initial projection and DSConv backbone\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                dilation=d,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Path 1: CNN-only with Mean+Max Pooling (Veritas SOTA inspired)\n        output_path1 = MeanMaxPoolingHead(\n            d_model=self.d_model,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n            name=\"cnn_only_head\"\n        )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Path 2: BiLSTM\
    \ with Additive Attention Pooling (Aetheria SOTA inspired)\n        output_path2 = BiLSTMAdditiveAttentionHead(\n            d_model=self.d_model,\n            lstm_hidden_dim=self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n            name=\"hybrid_bilstm_head\"\n        )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Learnable scalar alpha for linear blending\n        learnable_alpha_logit = self.param('alpha_logit', nn.initializers.constant(self.alpha_init_val), ())\n        alpha = nn.sigmoid(learnable_alpha_logit) # Ensure alpha is between 0 and 1\n\n        # Blended output\n        blended_output = alpha * output_path1 + (1 - alpha) * output_path2\n\n        # Final MLP Head (shared for blended output)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(blended_output)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type\
    \ == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = GatedDualPathNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# =========================\n# Station\
    \ hooks\n# =========================\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False, # Explicitly False\n        'alpha_init_val': 0.0 # For nn.sigmoid(alpha_logit) to be 0.5 initially\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n\
    \        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n        alpha_init_val=hparams.get('alpha_init_val', 0.0),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward\
    \ pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation\
    \ works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0136 |  0.4107  | 0.4107 \n 20  | 0.0088 |  0.4968  | 0.4968 \n 30  | 0.0033 |  0.4428  | 0.4968 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 30 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4968 Time:29s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.4968286954357026\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.496829\nTraining time: 39s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\n\
    Epoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0545  | 0.0545 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0347  | 0.0545 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0545 Time:99s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.054538001347940644\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.054538\nTraining time: 109s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1517 |  0.8711  | 0.8770 \n 20  | 0.1074 |  0.8784  | 0.8943 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 25 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.8943 Time:1126s\n[Complete] MRL val_metric=0.8943080902099609\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.894308\nTraining time: 1141s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0354 |  0.5617  | 0.5617 \n 20  | 0.0304 |  0.5393  | 0.5647 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 22 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5647 Time:1358s\n[Complete] PRS val_metric=0.5646980404853821\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.564698\nTraining time: 1374s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification,\
    \ accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1608 |  0.9246  | 0.9246 \n 20  | 0.0559 |  0.9415  | 0.9415 \n 30  | 0.0309 |  0.9323  | 0.9415 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 30 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9415 Time:1466s\n[Complete] ncRNA val_metric=0.9415384615384615\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.941538\nTraining time: 1477s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0658 |  0.9527  | 0.9528 \n=============================================\n\
    Timeout epoch 11\n=============================================\nBest:0.9528 Time:1803s\n[Complete] Modif val_metric=0.9528257791424193\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.952826\nTraining time: 1822s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: ea3589d0-81bc-44bc-8097-13420fc8a490\nTotal time: 1867s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 10:23:08,813\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761099788814026165\n2025-10-22 10:23:08,828\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761099788828489262\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence\
    \ Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 198 | 1 | Dispatcher v3: Optimal Specialist (Monolithic CNN for CRI-Off) | Axiom I | 119 | 0.6555 | 0.8412 | 0.0769 | 0.4967 | 0.7875 | 0.9504 | 0.5482 | 0.8877 |\n| 197 | 1 | Precise SOTA Replication: Aetheria's Gated Dual-Path (ID 187) | Veritas I | 119 | 0.6804 | 0.8583 | 0.0545 | 0.4968 | 0.8943 | 0.9528 | 0.5647 | 0.9415 |\n| 196 | 1 | Dispatcher v2: Upgraded Siamese Specialist with Hybrid Encoder | Axiom I | 117 | 0.6587 | 0.8456 | 0.0618 | 0.5165 | 0.7885 | 0.9508 | 0.5535 | 0.8938 |\n| 195 | 1 | SOTA Rerun: Gated Dual-Path Feature Fusion (Veritas SOTA) + (Aetheria SOTA) | Veritas I | 117 |\
    \ 0.6753 | 0.8520 | 0.0574 | 0.4609 | 0.8895 | 0.9529 | 0.5665 | 0.9477 |\n| 194 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path with Backbone-Feature MLP Gate (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 116 | 0.6790 | 0.8545 | 0.0654 | 0.4733 | 0.8957 | 0.9514 | 0.5666 | 0.9462 |\n| 193 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path Feature Fusion: Veritas SOTA (DSConv-HybridPool) + Aetheria SOTA (DSConv-BiLSTM-A... | Veritas I | 115 | 0.6805 | 0.8559 | 0.0640 | 0.4926 | 0.8899 | 0.9529 | 0.5622 | 0.9462 |\n| 192 | 1 | Task-Aware Dispatcher: Hybrid Generalist and Siamese Specialist | Axiom I | 114 | 0.6618 | 0.8433 | 0.0707 | 0.5091 | 0.8153 | 0.9507 | 0.5389 | 0.9046 |\n| 191 | 1 | Replication: Gated Dual-Path (No-PE) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 114 | 0.6787 | 0.8627 | 0.0556 | 0.4780 | 0.8897 | 0.9521 | 0.5652 | 0.9477 |\n| 190 | 1 | Replication: Gated Dual-Path (No-PE) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 114 | 0.6809 | 0.8585 | 0.0563 | 0.4972 | 0.8909 | 0.9513 | 0.5659 | 0.9462 |\n| 189 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path with Adaptive MLP Gate (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 113 | 0.6765 |\
    \ 0.8621 | 0.0530 | 0.4807 | 0.8803 | 0.9528 | 0.5587 | 0.9477 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
